{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural-amp","type":"ConceptScheme","prefLabel":{"en":"Geomorphological natural feature - extended","es":"Objeto geomorfológico natural - ampliado"},"description":{"es":"Términos referidos al objeto geomorfológico natural."},"publisher":{"id":"https://www.igme.es/"},"created":"2026-03-01","modified":"2026-03-01","creator":"https://commission.europa.eu/","provenance":"Términos originales de INSPIRE","versionInfo":"1.0.0","license":{"id":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"},"hasTopConcept":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/base-de-montaña","prefLabel":{"en":"mountainbase","es":"base de montaña"},"definition":{"en":"A geomorphologic component of mountains consisting of the strongly to slightly concave colluvial apron or wedge at the bottom of mountain slopes.","es":"Elemento geomorfológico de una montaña constituido por una falda o cuña coluvial, firme o aproximadamente cóncava, situada al pie de las pendientes."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/base-del-talud","prefLabel":{"en":"base slope","es":"base del talud"},"definition":{"en":"A geomorphologic component of hills consisting of the concave to linear slope (perpendicular to the contour) which, regardless of the lateral shape, is an area that forms an apron or wedge at the bottom of a hillside dominated by colluvial and slope wash processes and sediments","es":"Elemento geomorfológico de una colina constituido por una pendiente cóncava lineal (perpendicular al contorno) que, independientemente de la pendiente lateral, forma un saliente o cuña al pie de una colina, dominado por procesos coluviales y de lavado de la pendiente y por la deposición de sedimentos"}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cara-desnuda","prefLabel":{"en":"free face","es":"cara desnuda"},"definition":{"en":"A geomorphologic component of hills and mountains consisting of an outcrop of bare rock that sheds rock fragments and other sediments to, and commonly stands more steeply than the angle of repose of, the colluvial slope immediately below; most commonly found on shoulder and back slope positions, and can comprise part or all of a nose slope or side slope.","es":"Elemento geomorfológico de una colina o montaña constituido por un afloramiento de roca desnuda que suele ser más empinado que el ángulo de reposo, y que proporciona fragmentos de roca y otros sedimentos a la pendiente coluvial situada inmediatamente debajo; generalmente aparece en la ladera de menor pendiente y puede incluir una parte o la totalidad de una ladera divergente o una cuesta."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cima-de-montaña","prefLabel":{"en":"mountaintop","es":"cima de montaña"},"definition":{"en":"A geomorphologic component of mountains consisting of the uppermost, comparatively level or gently sloped area of mountains, characterized by relatively short, simple slopes composed of bare rock, residuum, or short-transport colluvial sediments.","es":"Elemento geomorfológico de una montaña constituido por el nivel relativamente más elevado y caracterizado por pendientes relativamente cortas y sencillas compuestas por roca desnuda, residuos o sedimentos coluviales transportados desde corta distancia."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/colina","prefLabel":{"en":"hill","es":"colina"},"definition":{"en":"A generic term for an elevated area of the land surface, rising at least 30 metres to as much as 300 metres above surrounding lowlands, usually with a nominal summit area relative to bounding slopes, a well-defined, rounded outline and slopes that generally exceed 15 percent.","es":"Término genérico que designa un área elevada de la superficie terrestre, que se alza entre 30 y 300 metros sobre las tierras bajas circundantes y que presenta generalmente una cumbre nominal en relación con sus laderas, una silueta redondeada bien definida y pendientes que superan en general el 15 por ciento."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cresta","prefLabel":{"en":"crest","es":"cresta"},"definition":{"en":"A geomorphologic component of hills consisting of the convex slopes (perpendicular to the contour) that form the narrow, roughly linear top area of a hill, ridge, or other upland where shoulders have converged to the extent that little or no summit remains; dominated by erosion, slope wash and mass movement processes and sediments","es":"Elemento geomorfológico de una colina constituido por unas laderas convexas (perpendiculares al contorno) que convergen para formar la parte superior, estrecha y generalmente lineal, de la colina, cordillera o tierra alta, hasta el punto de que apenas subsiste una cumbre; está dominada por los procesos de erosión, lavado de laderas y movimiento de masas, y por los sedimentos"}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cuesta","prefLabel":{"en":"side slope","es":"cuesta"},"definition":{"en":"A geomorphologic component of hills consisting of a laterally planar area of a hillside, resulting in predominantly parallel overland water flow. Contour lines generally form straight lines.","es":"Elemento geomorfológico de una colina constituido por un área de la ladera lateralmente plana que determina que las corrientes de agua sean predominantemente paralelas. Las curvas de nivel son en general rectas."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/depresion","prefLabel":{"en":"depression","es":"depresión"},"definition":{"en":"Any relatively sunken part of the Earth's surface; especially a low-lying area surrounded by higher ground.","es":"Parte relativamente hundida de la superficie terrestre; especialmente, área baja rodeada de tierras más altas."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/forma-erosiva","prefLabel":{"en":"destructional feature","es":"forma erosiva"},"definition":{"en":"Site of a landform that owes its origin, form, position, or general character to the removal of material by erosion and weathering (degradation) processes resulting from the wearing-down or away of the land surface.","es":"Forma de relieve que debe su origen, su forma, su posición o su carácter general a procesos de eliminación de material por erosión o meteorización (degradación) resultantes del desgaste de la superficie terrestre."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/formacion-superficial","prefLabel":{"en":"constructional feature","es":"formación superficial"},"definition":{"en":"Site of a landform that owes its origin, form, position, or general character to depositional (aggradational) processes, such as the accumulation of sediment","es":"Forma de relieve que debe su origen, su forma, su posición o su carácter general a procesos de deposición (agradación), como la acumulación de sedimentos"}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/interfluvio","prefLabel":{"en":"interfluve","es":"interfluvio"},"definition":{"en":"A geomorphologic component of hills consisting of the uppermost, comparatively level or gently sloped area of a hill; shoulders of back wearing hill slopes can narrow the upland or merge resulting in a strongly convex shape.","es":"Elemento geomorfológico de una colina constituido por el nivel relativamente más elevado o el área de pendiente más suave; las laderas pueden estrechar la zona superior o unirse para dar una forma muy convexa."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/ladera","prefLabel":{"en":"mountainflank","es":"ladera"},"definition":{"en":"A geomorphologic component of mountains characterized by very long, complex back slopes with comparatively high slope gradients and composed of highly-diverse colluvial sediment mantles, rock outcrops or structural benches.","es":"Elemento geomorfológico de una montaña caracterizado por pendientes muy largas y complejas con gradientes relativamente elevados y compuestas por mantos de sedimentos coluviales muy variados, afloramientos de roca y resaltes estructurales."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/ladera-divergente","prefLabel":{"en":"nose slope","es":"ladera divergente"},"definition":{"en":"A geomorphologic component of hills consisting of the projecting end (laterally convex area) of a hillside, resulting in predominantly divergent overland water flow; contour lines generally form convex curves.","es":"Elemento geomorfológico de una colina constituido por un extremo saliente (generalmente un área convexa) de la ladera, que determina que las corrientes de agua sean predominantemente divergentes; las curvas de nivel son en general curvas convexas."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/llanura","prefLabel":{"en":"plain","es":"llanura"},"definition":{"en":"Any flat area, large or small, at a low elevation; specifically an extensive region of comparatively smooth and level or gently undulaing land, having few or no prominent surface irregularities but sometimes having a considerable slope, and usually at a low elevation with reference to surrounding areas.","es":"Área plana, grande o pequeña, de baja elevación; específicamente, una región extensa de tierra relativamente nivelada o poco ondulada, con pocas o ninguna irregularidad superficial, aunque a veces con una considerable pendiente, y generalmente con una baja elevación en relación con las áreas circundantes."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/modelo-de-drenaje","prefLabel":{"en":"drainage pattern","es":"modelo de drenaje"},"definition":{"en":"The configuration or arrangement of stream courses in an area, including gullies or first-order channelized flow areas, higher order tributaries, and main streams.","es":"Configuración o disposición de los cursos de agua en una zona, incluidos los barrancos o cursos canalizados de primer orden, los afluentes de orden superior y los cursos de agua principales."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/montaña","prefLabel":{"en":"mountain","es":"montaña"},"definition":{"en":"A generic term for an elevated area of the land surface, rising more than 300 metres above surrounding lowlands, usually with a nominal summit area relative to bounding slopes and generally with steep sides (greater than 25 percent slope) with or without considerable bare-rock exposed.","es":"Término genérico que designa un área elevada de la superficie terrestre, que se levanta más de 300 metros sobre las tierras bajas circundantes y presenta generalmente una cumbre definida en relación con sus laderas y pendientes que suelen ser empinadas (más del 25 por ciento), con o sin exposición considerable de roca desnuda."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/objeto-degradativo","prefLabel":{"en":"degradation feature","es":"objeto degradativo"},"definition":{"en":"A geomorphologic feature resulting from the wearing down or away, and the general lowering or reduction, of the Earth's surface by natural processes of weathering and erosion, and which may infer the processes of transportation of sediment.","es":"Objeto geomorfológico resultante del desgaste, y en general la reducción, de la superficie terrestre por procesos naturales de meteorización y erosión y que puede inducir procesos de transporte de sedimentos."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/objeto-erosionado","prefLabel":{"en":"erosional features","es":"objeto erosionado"},"definition":{"en":"A land surface shaped by the action of erosion, especially by running water.","es":"Superficie del terreno configurada por la acción de la erosión, sobre todo del agua corriente."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/objeto-exhumado","prefLabel":{"en":"exhumed feature","es":"objeto exhumado"},"definition":{"en":"Formerly buried landforms, geomorphologic surfaces, or paleosols that have been re-exposed by erosion of the covering mantle.","es":"Forma del relieve, superficie geomorfológica o paleosuelo previmente enterrado que queda de nuevo expuesto por erosión del manto que lo cubría."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/objeto-fosilizado","prefLabel":{"en":"buried feature","es":"objeto fosilizado"},"definition":{"en":"Landforms, geomorphologic surfaces, or paleosols covered by younger sediments.","es":"Forma del relieve, superficie geomorfológica o paleosuelo cubierto por sedimentos más jóvenes."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/objeto-geomorfologico-natural","prefLabel":{"en":"natural geomorphologic feature","es":"objeto geomorfológico natural"},"definition":{"en":"A geomorphologic feature produced by the natural dynamics.","es":"Objeto geomorfológico producido por la dinámica natural."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/objetos-de-impacto","prefLabel":{"en":"impact features","es":"objetos de impacto"},"definition":{"en":"Geomorphologic landscapes and landforms related to the impact of extraterrestrial material on the Earth's surface.","es":"Paisajes geomorfológicos y formas del relieve relacionados con el impacto de objetos extraterrestres sobre la superficie terrestre."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/objetos-eolicos","prefLabel":{"en":"eolian features","es":"objetos eólicos"},"definition":{"en":"Geomorphologic landscapes and landforms related to wind-dominated environments.","es":"Paisajes geomorfológicos y formas del relieve relativos a entornos dominados por el viento."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/arenas-eolicas-manto-eolico","prefLabel":{"en":"aeolian sands; sand sheet","es":"arenas eólicas; manto eólico"},"definition":{"en":"Extensive deposit of wind-transported sand.","es":"Depósito extenso de arena transportada por el viento."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/campo-de-dunas-cordon-de-dunas","prefLabel":{"en":"dune field; dune ridge","es":"campo de dunas; cordón de dunas"},"definition":{"en":"Area with sand accumulations formed by the wind.","es":"Zona con acumulaciones de arena formadas por el viento."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/campo-de-dunas-con-vegetacion","prefLabel":{"en":"vegetated dune field","es":"campo de dunas con vegetación"},"definition":{"en":"A dune field partially or totally stabilized by vegetation.","es":"Campo de dunas parcial o totalmente estabilizado por vegetación."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/campo-de-dunas-fosiles","prefLabel":{"en":"fossil dune field","es":"campo de dunas fósiles"},"definition":{"en":"A field of inactive, fixed and consolidated dunes.","es":"Campo de dunas inactivas, fijadas y consolidadas."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cresta-dunar","prefLabel":{"en":"dune crest","es":"cresta dunar"},"definition":{"en":"The highest line of a dune.","es":"Línea más alta de una duna."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cubetas-de-deflaccion","prefLabel":{"en":"deflation hollows","es":"cubetas de deflacción"},"definition":{"en":"Shallow depressions excavated by wind action.","es":"Depresiones poco profundas excavadas por la acción del viento."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/dunas","prefLabel":{"en":"dunes","es":"dunas"},"definition":{"en":"Sand mounds formed by wind action.","es":"Montículos de arena formados por acción eólica."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/barjanes","prefLabel":{"en":"barchans","es":"barjanes"},"definition":{"en":"Crescent-shaped dunes with horns pointing downwind.","es":"Dunas en forma de media luna con las puntas orientadas a sotavento."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/dunas-longitudinales","prefLabel":{"en":"longitudinal dunes","es":"dunas longitudinales"},"definition":{"en":"Elongated dunes parallel to the wind direction.","es":"Dunas alargadas paralelas a la dirección del viento."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/dunas-parabolicas","prefLabel":{"en":"parabolic dunes","es":"dunas parabólicas"},"definition":{"en":"U-shaped or parabolic dunes open in the wind direction.","es":"Dunas con forma de U o parábola abiertas en la dirección del viento."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/dunas-transversales","prefLabel":{"en":"transverse dunes","es":"dunas transversales"},"definition":{"en":"Elongated dunes perpendicular to the wind direction.","es":"Dunas alargadas perpendiculares a la dirección del viento."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/dunas-trepadoras","prefLabel":{"en":"climbing dunes","es":"dunas trepadoras"},"definition":{"en":"Dunes that climb up a slope driven by the wind.","es":"Dunas que ascienden por una ladera empujadas por el viento."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/loess","prefLabel":{"en":"loess","es":"loess"},"definition":{"en":"A deposit of silt transported and deposited by the wind.","es":"Depósito de limo transportado y depositado por el viento."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/ventifactos","prefLabel":{"en":"ventifacts","es":"ventifactos"},"definition":{"en":"Pebbles with polished faces and facets produced by wind abrasion.","es":"Cantos con caras pulidas y facetas producidas por abrasión eólica."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/viento-dominante","prefLabel":{"en":"prevailing wind","es":"viento dominante"},"definition":{"en":"Predominant wind direction in an area.","es":"Dirección predominante del viento en una zona."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/objetos-geograficos-aluviales-y-fluviales","prefLabel":{"en":"alluvial and fluvial features","es":"objetos geográficos aluviales y fluviales"},"definition":{"en":"Geomorphologic landscapes and landforms dominantly related to concentrated water flow (channel flow).","es":"Paisajes geomorfológicos y formas del relieve relacionados predominantemente con corrientes de agua concentradas (corrientes canalizadas)."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/abanico-aluvial-de-baja-pendiente","prefLabel":{"en":"low-gradient alluvial fan","es":"abanico aluvial de baja pendiente"},"definition":{"en":"An alluvial fan of great extent and low gradient.","es":"Abanico aluvial de gran extensión y baja pendiente."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/albardon-dique-natural-levee","prefLabel":{"en":"natural levee","es":"albardón; dique natural; levée"},"definition":{"en":"An elongated elevation along river margins formed by overbank flooding.","es":"Elevación alargada a lo largo de las márgenes de un río formada por desbordamiento."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/arista-o-divisoria-montanyosa","prefLabel":{"en":"mountain ridge; divide","es":"arista o divisoria montañosa"},"definition":{"en":"A narrow and sharp crest separating drainage basins in mountainous areas.","es":"Cresta estrecha y aguda que separa cuencas hidrográficas en zonas montañosas."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/aristas-en-interfluvios","prefLabel":{"en":"interfluve ridges","es":"aristas en interfluvios"},"definition":{"en":"Sharp ridges separating adjacent fluvial channels.","es":"Crestas agudas que separan cauces fluviales adyacentes."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/arroyada-en-regueros-permanentes-o-cambiantes","prefLabel":{"en":"rill wash","es":"arroyada en regueros, permanentes o cambiantes"},"definition":{"en":"Surface erosion by concentrated flow in small rills.","es":"Erosión superficial por flujo concentrado en pequeños surcos."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/banco-barra","prefLabel":{"en":"bank; bar","es":"banco; barra"},"definition":{"en":"Sediment accumulation within a river channel.","es":"Acumulación de sedimentos en el interior de un cauce fluvial."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/banco-barra-con-cicatrices-de-acrecion-lateral","prefLabel":{"en":"bar with lateral accretion scars","es":"banco; barra con cicatrices de acreción lateral"},"definition":{"en":"A fluvial bar with visible marks of lateral growth.","es":"Barra fluvial con marcas visibles de crecimiento lateral."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/borde-de-terraza-en-niveles-solapados","prefLabel":{"en":"overlapping terrace levels edge","es":"borde de terraza en niveles solapados"},"definition":{"en":"Edge of fluvial terraces that overlap in their lateral extent.","es":"Borde de terrazas fluviales que se solapan en su extensión lateral."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cambio-brusco-de-pendiente-salto-de-agua-cascada","prefLabel":{"en":"waterfall; cascade","es":"cambio brusco de pendiente; salto de agua; cascada"},"definition":{"en":"Vertical or near-vertical water drop in a river channel.","es":"Caída vertical o casi vertical del agua en un cauce fluvial."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cambio-de-pendiente-rapidos","prefLabel":{"en":"slope change; rapids","es":"cambio de pendiente; rápidos"},"definition":{"en":"Zone of slope increase in a river channel with turbulent flow.","es":"Zona de aumento de pendiente en un cauce fluvial con flujo turbulento."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/canal-principal-cauce-activo-en-grandes-rios-limite-del-lecho","prefLabel":{"en":"main channel; active bed limit","es":"canal principal; cauce activo en grandes ríos; límite del lecho"},"definition":{"en":"Main channel of a river or limit of the active bed.","es":"Cauce principal de un río o límite del lecho activo."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/canal-temporal-o-de-avenida-brazo-de-corriente-aliviadero-chute","prefLabel":{"en":"flood channel; chute","es":"canal temporal o de avenida, brazo de corriente, aliviadero; chute"},"definition":{"en":"A channel that only functions during floods.","es":"Canal que solo funciona durante crecidas o avenidas."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/captura-fluvial","prefLabel":{"en":"river capture","es":"captura fluvial"},"definition":{"en":"Process by which a river diverts the waters of another by eroding its divide.","es":"Proceso por el cual un río desvía las aguas de otro al erosionar su divisoria."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/carcavas","prefLabel":{"en":"gullies","es":"cárcavas"},"definition":{"en":"Deep and narrow incisions in soft materials produced by concentrated water erosion.","es":"Incisiones profundas y estrechas en materiales blandos producidas por erosión hídrica concentrada."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/area-acarcavada","prefLabel":{"en":"gullied area","es":"área acarcavada"},"definition":{"en":"An area with a high density of gullies.","es":"Zona con una alta densidad de cárcavas."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cabecera-de-carcavas","prefLabel":{"en":"gully head","es":"cabecera de cárcavas"},"definition":{"en":"Upper part of a gully where erosional retreat occurs.","es":"Parte superior de una cárcava donde se produce el retroceso erosivo."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/carcavas-puntual","prefLabel":{"en":"gully (point feature)","es":"cárcavas (puntual)"},"definition":{"en":"Point representation of an individual gully.","es":"Representación puntual de una cárcava individual."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cauce-o-meandro-abandonado","prefLabel":{"en":"abandoned channel; abandoned meander","es":"cauce o meandro abandonado"},"definition":{"en":"A former channel or meander that is no longer functional.","es":"Antiguo cauce o meandro que ya no es funcional."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cauce-o-meandro-abandonado-temporalmente-inundado-oxbow","prefLabel":{"en":"oxbow lake","es":"cauce o meandro abandonado, temporalmente inundado; oxbow"},"definition":{"en":"An abandoned meander that temporarily floods forming an oxbow lake.","es":"Meandro abandonado que se inunda temporalmente formando un lago en herradura."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/collado","prefLabel":{"en":"pass; col","es":"collado; puerto; col"},"definition":{"en":"A depression in a divide allowing passage.","es":"Depresión en una divisoria que permite el paso."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/confluencia-anomala-de-cauces","prefLabel":{"en":"anomalous channel confluence","es":"confluencia anómala de cauces"},"definition":{"en":"Junction of fluvial channels with an unusual angle or arrangement suggesting structural control.","es":"Unión de cauces fluviales con un ángulo o disposición inusual que sugiere control estructural."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cono-de-deyeccion-abanico-aluvial-con-pendiente-elevada","prefLabel":{"en":"alluvial fan; high-gradient fan","es":"cono de deyección; abanico aluvial con pendiente elevada"},"definition":{"en":"Cone-shaped deposit at the foot of a mountain formed by torrential streams.","es":"Depósito en forma de cono al pie de una montaña formado por corrientes torrenciales."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cuerda-o-divisoria-montanyosa-redondeada","prefLabel":{"en":"rounded mountain divide","es":"cuerda o divisoria montañosa redondeada"},"definition":{"en":"A watershed divide with a rounded and gentle profile.","es":"Divisoria de aguas con perfil redondeado y suave."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/deposito-de-arroyada-aluvial-coluvial-relleno-de-vaguada","prefLabel":{"en":"wash deposit; alluvial-colluvial fill","es":"depósito de arroyada; aluvial-coluvial; relleno de vaguada"},"definition":{"en":"Deposit formed by diffuse wash in thalwegs and slopes.","es":"Depósito formado por arroyada difusa en vaguadas y laderas."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/derrame-de-canal-crevasse-splay","prefLabel":{"en":"crevasse splay","es":"derrame de canal; crevasse splay"},"definition":{"en":"Fan-shaped deposit formed by the breach of a river natural levee.","es":"Depósito en abanico formado por la rotura del dique natural de un río."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/divisoria-de-aguas-poco-definida","prefLabel":{"en":"poorly defined watershed","es":"divisoria de aguas poco definida"},"definition":{"en":"A watershed divide with a diffuse trace, difficult to locate precisely.","es":"Divisoria de aguas de trazado difuso y difícil de localizar con precisión."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/erosion-lateral-zapamiento-socavamiento","prefLabel":{"en":"lateral erosion; undercutting","es":"erosión lateral; zapamiento; socavamiento"},"definition":{"en":"Erosion acting horizontally on the banks of a channel.","es":"Erosión que actúa horizontalmente sobre las márgenes de un cauce."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe-fluvial","prefLabel":{"en":"fluvial scarp","es":"escarpe fluvial"},"definition":{"en":"Vertical or subvertical slope carved by river erosive action.","es":"Talud vertical o subvertical tallado por la acción erosiva de un río."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe-entre-25-100-metros","prefLabel":{"en":"scarp 25-100 m","es":"escarpe entre 25-100 metros"},"definition":{"en":"A fluvial scarp between 25 and 100 metres high.","es":"Escarpe fluvial de entre 25 y 100 metros de altura."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe-inferior-a-25-metros","prefLabel":{"en":"scarp less than 25 m","es":"escarpe inferior a 25 metros"},"definition":{"en":"A fluvial scarp less than 25 metres high.","es":"Escarpe fluvial de menos de 25 metros de altura."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe-superior-a-100-metros","prefLabel":{"en":"scarp over 100 m","es":"escarpe superior a 100 metros"},"definition":{"en":"A fluvial scarp over 100 metres high.","es":"Escarpe fluvial de más de 100 metros de altura."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe-o-borde-de-terraza-colgada-e-indicacion-de-cota-en-metros","prefLabel":{"en":"hanging terrace scarp with elevation in metres","es":"escarpe o borde de terraza colgada e indicación de cota en metros"},"definition":{"en":"Edge of a hanging fluvial terrace with elevation indication.","es":"Borde de una terraza fluvial colgada con indicación de su cota."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe-o-borde-de-terraza-degradado","prefLabel":{"en":"degraded terrace scarp","es":"escarpe o borde de terraza degradado"},"definition":{"en":"Fluvial terrace edge smoothed by erosional processes.","es":"Borde de terraza fluvial suavizado por procesos erosivos."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/fondo-de-rambla-torrencial","prefLabel":{"en":"ephemeral stream bed","es":"fondo de rambla torrencial"},"definition":{"en":"Bed of a torrential watercourse with intermittent flow.","es":"Lecho de un curso de agua torrencial con flujo intermitente."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/fondo-de-valle","prefLabel":{"en":"valley floor","es":"fondo de valle"},"definition":{"en":"The lowest and generally flat part of a fluvial valley.","es":"Parte más baja y generalmente plana de un valle fluvial."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/fondo-de-valle-colgado","prefLabel":{"en":"hanging valley floor","es":"fondo de valle colgado"},"definition":{"en":"Flat floor of a valley hanging above the main valley.","es":"Fondo plano de un valle colgado respecto al valle principal."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/garganta-canyon-fluvial-desfiladero","prefLabel":{"en":"gorge; fluvial canyon","es":"garganta; cañón fluvial; desfiladero"},"definition":{"en":"A very narrow and deep valley with vertical or subvertical walls.","es":"Valle muy estrecho y profundo con paredes verticales o subverticales."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/hombrera","prefLabel":{"en":"shoulder; bench","es":"hombrera; rellano"},"definition":{"en":"A subhorizontal surface interrupting a slope.","es":"Superficie subhorizontal que interrumpe una pendiente."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/incision-dominada-por-sufusion-piping","prefLabel":{"en":"piping-dominated incision","es":"incisión dominada por sufusión; piping"},"definition":{"en":"Terrain incision dominated by internal erosion processes (piping).","es":"Incisión del terreno dominada por procesos de erosión interna (piping)."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/incision-lineal-en-cuna-vaguada","prefLabel":{"en":"wedge-shaped incision; thalweg","es":"incisión lineal en cuna; vaguada"},"definition":{"en":"Fluvial incision with a wedge-shaped or poorly developed flat-bottom cross section.","es":"Incisión fluvial de perfil transversal en cuña o fondo plano poco desarrollado."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/incision-lineal-en-v-barranco","prefLabel":{"en":"V-shaped incision; ravine","es":"incisión lineal en v; barranco"},"definition":{"en":"Fluvial incision with a V-shaped cross section.","es":"Incisión fluvial de perfil transversal en forma de V."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/linea-de-drenaje-difusa","prefLabel":{"en":"diffuse drainage line","es":"línea de drenaje difusa"},"definition":{"en":"A runoff line without a defined channel.","es":"Línea de escorrentía sin cauce definido."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/llanura-de-inundacion","prefLabel":{"en":"floodplain","es":"llanura de inundación"},"definition":{"en":"A flat surface adjacent to a river that is periodically flooded.","es":"Superficie plana adyacente a un río que se inunda periódicamente."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/manantial","prefLabel":{"en":"spring","es":"manantial"},"definition":{"en":"Natural emergence of groundwater at the surface.","es":"Surgencia natural de agua subterránea en la superficie."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/perdida-de-drenaje","prefLabel":{"en":"drainage loss","es":"pérdida de drenaje"},"definition":{"en":"Point where a river channel loses water by infiltration.","es":"Punto donde un cauce fluvial pierde agua por infiltración."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/surgencia-por-sufusion-piping","prefLabel":{"en":"piping spring","es":"surgencia por sufusión; piping"},"definition":{"en":"Water emergence produced by internal terrain erosion.","es":"Surgencia de agua producida por erosión interna del terreno."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/terraza","prefLabel":{"en":"terrace","es":"terraza"},"definition":{"en":"A flat surface elevated above the current channel, representing a former river level.","es":"Superficie plana elevada respecto al cauce actual, que representa un antiguo nivel del río."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/terraza-erosiva","prefLabel":{"en":"erosional terrace","es":"terraza erosiva"},"definition":{"en":"A terrace carved into rock without significant alluvial deposit.","es":"Terraza tallada en la roca sin depósito aluvial significativo."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/terraza-no-ciclica-de-encajamiento-convergente","prefLabel":{"en":"non-cyclic terrace (entrenching; convergent)","es":"terraza no cíclica (de encajamiento; convergente)"},"definition":{"en":"Terrace formed by progressive entrenchment without relation to climatic cycles.","es":"Terraza formada por encajamiento progresivo sin relación con ciclos climáticos."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/terraza-travertinica","prefLabel":{"en":"travertine terrace","es":"terraza travertínica"},"definition":{"en":"Terrace formed by calcium carbonate (travertine) precipitation.","es":"Terraza formada por precipitación de carbonato cálcico (travertino)."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/valle-colgado","prefLabel":{"en":"hanging valley","es":"valle colgado"},"definition":{"en":"A tributary valley whose floor is at a higher elevation than the main valley.","es":"Valle tributario cuyo fondo se encuentra a una cota más elevada que el valle principal."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/valle-o-vaguada-con-fondo-plano","prefLabel":{"en":"flat-bottomed valley","es":"valle o vaguada con fondo plano"},"definition":{"en":"A fluvial valley with a flat bottom occupied by alluvial deposits.","es":"Valle fluvial con fondo plano ocupado por depósitos aluviales."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/objetos-geograficos-karsticos-y-de-meteorizacion-quimica","prefLabel":{"en":"karst and chemical weathering features","es":"objetos geográficos kársticos y de meteorización química"},"definition":{"en":"Geomorphologic landscapes and landforms dominated by mineral dissolution, and commonly, subsurface drainage.","es":"Paisajes geomorfológicos y formas del relieve dominados por la disolución de minerales y, en general, por el drenaje subsuperficial."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/aplanamiento-karstico-superficie-de-corrosion","prefLabel":{"en":"karst planation surface","es":"aplanamiento kárstico; superficie de corrosión"},"definition":{"en":"A flat surface resulting from widespread karst dissolution.","es":"Superficie plana resultante de la disolución kárstica generalizada."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/area-con-relieves-residuales-karsticos-hums","prefLabel":{"en":"karst residual relief area; hums","es":"área con relieves residuales kársticos; hums"},"definition":{"en":"An area with abundant karst residual reliefs.","es":"Zona con abundantes relieves residuales kársticos."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/arenizacion-lehm-granitico","prefLabel":{"en":"arenization; granitic lehm","es":"arenización; lehm granítico"},"definition":{"en":"Weathering that transforms granitic rock into sand or lehm.","es":"Meteorización que transforma la roca granítica en arena o lehm."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/argilizaciones","prefLabel":{"en":"argillization","es":"argilizaciones"},"definition":{"en":"Transformation of minerals into clay by chemical weathering.","es":"Transformación de minerales en arcilla por meteorización química."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/berrocal","prefLabel":{"en":"boulder field; tor field","es":"berrocal"},"definition":{"en":"An area with abundant residual granite boulders.","es":"Zona con abundantes bolos graníticos residuales."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/bolos","prefLabel":{"en":"boulders; corestones","es":"bolos"},"definition":{"en":"Rounded residual blocks produced by spheroidal weathering.","es":"Bloques redondeados residuales producidos por meteorización esferoidal."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/canyon-garganta-desfiladero","prefLabel":{"en":"canyon; gorge","es":"cañón; garganta; desfiladero"},"definition":{"en":"A very deep and narrow valley with vertical walls in karst terrain.","es":"Valle muy profundo y estrecho con paredes verticales en terreno kárstico."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/caolinizaciones","prefLabel":{"en":"kaolinization","es":"caolinizaciones"},"definition":{"en":"Transformation of feldspars into kaolinite group minerals.","es":"Transformación de feldespatos en minerales del grupo de la caolinita."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/carbonataciones","prefLabel":{"en":"carbonation","es":"carbonataciones"},"definition":{"en":"Formation of carbonate crusts or accumulations by precipitation.","es":"Formación de costras o acumulaciones de carbonato por precipitación."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cerro-ruiniforme","prefLabel":{"en":"ruiniform hill; block chaos","es":"cerro ruiniforme; caos de bloques"},"definition":{"en":"Relief with a ruin-like appearance due to weathering and dismantling.","es":"Relieve con aspecto de ruinas por meteorización y desmantelamiento."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cerro-ruiniforme-caos-de-bloques","prefLabel":{"en":"ruiniform hill; block chaos","es":"cerro ruiniforme poligenetico"},"altLabel":{"es":["caos de bloques"]},"definition":{"en":"Relief with a ruin-like appearance due to weathering and dismantling.","es":"Relieve con aspecto de ruinas por meteorización y desmantelamiento."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cueva","prefLabel":{"en":"cave","es":"cueva"},"definition":{"en":"A natural underground cavity of karst origin.","es":"Cavidad subterránea natural de origen kárstico."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/dolina","prefLabel":{"en":"doline; sinkhole","es":"dolina"},"definition":{"en":"A closed depression of circular or elliptical plan formed by karst dissolution.","es":"Depresión cerrada de planta circular o elíptica formada por disolución kárstica."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/dolina-capturada","prefLabel":{"en":"captured doline","es":"dolina capturada"},"definition":{"en":"A doline connected to surface drainage by capture.","es":"Dolina conectada al drenaje superficial por captura."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/dolina-con-borde-difuso","prefLabel":{"en":"doline with diffuse rim","es":"dolina con borde difuso"},"definition":{"en":"A doline whose rim has been smoothed by erosion.","es":"Dolina cuyo borde ha sido suavizado por erosión."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/dolina-con-fondo-plano","prefLabel":{"en":"flat-bottomed doline","es":"dolina con fondo plano"},"definition":{"en":"A doline with a horizontal bottom generally occupied by decalcification clays.","es":"Dolina con fondo horizontal ocupado generalmente por arcillas de descalcificación."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/dolina-de-hundimiento-o-dolina-en-ventana","prefLabel":{"en":"collapse doline; window doline","es":"dolina de hundimiento o dolina en ventana"},"definition":{"en":"A doline formed by collapse of the roof of an underground cavity.","es":"Dolina formada por colapso del techo de una cavidad subterránea."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/dolina-de-karst-cubierto-dolina-aluvial","prefLabel":{"en":"covered karst doline; alluvial doline","es":"dolina de karst cubierto; dolina aluvial"},"definition":{"en":"A doline formed in materials covering the underlying karst.","es":"Dolina formada en materiales que recubren el karst subyacente."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/dolina-en-embudo","prefLabel":{"en":"funnel-shaped doline","es":"dolina en embudo"},"definition":{"en":"A funnel-shaped doline with converging inclined walls.","es":"Dolina con forma de embudo y paredes inclinadas convergentes."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/pequenya-dolina","prefLabel":{"en":"small doline","es":"pequeña dolina"},"definition":{"en":"A doline of small dimensions.","es":"Dolina de dimensiones reducidas."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/campo-de-pequenyas-dolinas","prefLabel":{"en":"small doline field","es":"campo de pequeñas dolinas"},"definition":{"en":"An area with a high density of small dolines.","es":"Zona con alta densidad de dolinas de pequeño tamaño."}}]}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/domo-y-dorso-de-ballena","prefLabel":{"en":"dome and whaleback","es":"domo y dorso de ballena"},"definition":{"en":"A rounded form in bare rock produced by weathering.","es":"Forma redondeada en roca desnuda producida por meteorización."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/ferruginizaciones-rubefacciones","prefLabel":{"en":"ferruginization; rubefaction","es":"ferruginizaciones; rubefacciones"},"definition":{"en":"Iron oxide enrichment giving a reddish coloration to rock or soil.","es":"Enriquecimiento en óxidos de hierro que da coloración rojiza a la roca o suelo."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/lapiaz","prefLabel":{"en":"karren; lapiaz","es":"lapiaz"},"definition":{"en":"Dissolution forms on the surface of calcareous rocks.","es":"Formas de disolución en la superficie de rocas calcáreas."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/campo-de-lapiaces","prefLabel":{"en":"karren field","es":"campo de lapiaces"},"definition":{"en":"An area with extensive karren development.","es":"Zona con desarrollo extenso de lapiaces."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/lapiaz-cubierto","prefLabel":{"en":"covered karren","es":"lapiaz cubierto"},"definition":{"en":"Karren totally covered by soil, visible only in cross section.","es":"Lapiaz totalmente cubierto por suelo, visible solo en corte."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/lapiaz-semicubierto","prefLabel":{"en":"semi-covered karren","es":"lapiaz semicubierto"},"definition":{"en":"Karren partially covered by soil or vegetation.","es":"Lapiaz parcialmente cubierto por suelo o vegetación."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/limite-de-alveolo-de-alteracion-nava","prefLabel":{"en":"weathering depression limit; nava","es":"límite de alveolo de alteración; nava"},"definition":{"en":"Limit of a closed depression formed by intense chemical weathering.","es":"Límite de una depresión cerrada formada por meteorización química intensa."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/limite-de-area-con-intensa-karstificacion","prefLabel":{"en":"intensely karstified area limit","es":"límite de área con intensa karstificación"},"definition":{"en":"Limit of a zone with very advanced karst development.","es":"Límite de una zona con desarrollo kárstico muy avanzado."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/limite-de-cuenca-endorreica-de-origen-karstico","prefLabel":{"en":"karst endorheic basin limit","es":"límite de cuenca endorreica de origen kárstico"},"definition":{"en":"Limit of a basin without external drainage originated by karst processes.","es":"Límite de una cuenca sin drenaje externo originada por procesos kársticos."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/limite-de-paleopolje","prefLabel":{"en":"palaeo-polje limit","es":"límite de paleopolje"},"definition":{"en":"Limit of a former polje no longer functional.","es":"Límite de un antiguo polje ya no funcional."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/limite-de-polje-funcional","prefLabel":{"en":"functional polje limit","es":"límite de polje funcional"},"definition":{"en":"Limit of a currently functional polje with karst drainage.","es":"Límite de un polje actualmente funcional con drenaje kárstico."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/meteorizacion-en-general","prefLabel":{"en":"weathering (general)","es":"meteorización en general"},"definition":{"en":"Rock alteration processes by atmospheric and chemical agents.","es":"Procesos de alteración de la roca por agentes atmosféricos y químicos."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/microformas-de-alteracion","prefLabel":{"en":"weathering microforms","es":"microformas de alteración"},"definition":{"en":"Small-scale forms produced by weathering on rock surfaces.","es":"Formas de pequeña escala producidas por meteorización en superficies rocosas."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/ponor","prefLabel":{"en":"ponor","es":"ponor"},"definition":{"en":"An opening in rock through which water from a polje or karst depression drains underground.","es":"Abertura en la roca por donde el agua de un polje o depresión kárstica drena al subsuelo."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/puente-o-tunel-natural","prefLabel":{"en":"natural bridge or tunnel","es":"puente o túnel natural"},"definition":{"en":"A natural arch or tunnel in rock formed by karst dissolution or erosion.","es":"Arco o túnel natural en roca formado por disolución kárstica o erosión."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/relieve-karstico-hum","prefLabel":{"en":"karst relief; hum","es":"relieve kárstico; hum"},"definition":{"en":"Positive residual relief in a karst landscape.","es":"Relieve residual positivo en un paisaje kárstico."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/roca-aislada-pinaculo-rocoso-tor","prefLabel":{"en":"tor; isolated rock pillar","es":"roca aislada; pináculo rocoso; tor"},"definition":{"en":"An isolated residual relief formed by differential weathering.","es":"Relieve residual aislado formado por meteorización diferencial."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/sales","prefLabel":{"en":"salt deposits","es":"sales"},"definition":{"en":"Surface salt accumulations by evaporation.","es":"Acumulaciones de sales en superficie por evaporación."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/silicificaciones","prefLabel":{"en":"silicification","es":"silicificaciones"},"definition":{"en":"Replacement of original rock minerals by silica.","es":"Reemplazamiento por sílice de los minerales originales de la roca."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/sima","prefLabel":{"en":"pothole; shaft","es":"sima"},"definition":{"en":"A deep vertical cavity in karst terrain.","es":"Cavidad vertical profunda en terreno kárstico."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/sumidero","prefLabel":{"en":"swallow hole; sinkhole","es":"sumidero"},"definition":{"en":"Point where a surface watercourse disappears into the karst underground.","es":"Punto donde un curso de agua superficial desaparece en el subsuelo kárstico."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/surgencia","prefLabel":{"en":"karst spring; resurgence","es":"surgencia"},"definition":{"en":"Emergence point of karst groundwater at the surface.","es":"Punto de salida de aguas subterráneas kársticas a la superficie."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/tafoni","prefLabel":{"en":"tafoni","es":"tafoni"},"definition":{"en":"Weathering cavities on rock surfaces.","es":"Cavidades de meteorización en superficies rocosas."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/toba-travertino","prefLabel":{"en":"tufa; travertine","es":"toba; travertino"},"definition":{"en":"Calcium carbonate deposit precipitated by CO2-rich waters.","es":"Depósito de carbonato cálcico precipitado por aguas ricas en CO2."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/toba-masa-travertinica","prefLabel":{"en":"tufa; travertine mass","es":"toba; masa travertínica"},"definition":{"en":"A travertine mass or edifice of significant dimensions.","es":"Masa o edificio de travertino de dimensiones significativas."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/uvala","prefLabel":{"en":"uvala","es":"uvala"},"definition":{"en":"A larger karst depression formed by coalescence of several dolines.","es":"Depresión kárstica de mayor tamaño formada por coalescencia de varias dolinas."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/valle-ciego","prefLabel":{"en":"blind valley","es":"valle ciego"},"definition":{"en":"A fluvial valley that ends abruptly at a karst sinkhole.","es":"Valle fluvial que termina bruscamente en un sumidero kárstico."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/objetos-glaciales-fluvioglaciares-y-de-permafrost","prefLabel":{"en":"nival, periglacial and permafrost features","es":"objetos glaciales, fluvioglaciares y de permafrost"},"definition":{"en":"Geomorphologic landscapes and landforms related to snow, non-glacial, cold climate environments; geomorphologic landscapes and landforms occurring in the vicinity of glaciers and ice sheets; geomorphologic landscapes and landforms related to ground, soil, or rock that remains at or below 0º C for at least two years.","es":"Paisajes geomorfológicos y formas del relieve relativos a entornos de clima frío, con nieve, pero no glaciales; paisajes geomorfológicos y formas de relieve próximos a glaciares y placas de hielo; paisajes geomorfológicos y formas del relieve relativos a tierras, suelos o rocas que se mantienen a 0º C o menos durante dos años como mínimo."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/objetos-glaciales-glaciofluviales-glaciolacustres-y-glaciomarinos","prefLabel":{"en":"glacial, glaciofluvial, glaciolacustrine and glaciomarine features","es":"objetos glaciales, glaciofluviales, glaciolacustres y glaciomarinos"},"definition":{"en":"Geomorphologic landscapes and landforms related to to glacial, glaciofluvial, glaciolacustrine and glaciomarine environments.","es":"Paisajes geomorfológicos y formas del relieve relativos a entornos glaciales, glaciofluviales, glaciolacustres y glaciomarinos."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/acumulacion-de-origen-glaciar-indiferenciada-till","prefLabel":{"en":"undifferentiated glacial deposit; till","es":"acumulación de origen glaciar indiferenciada; till"},"definition":{"en":"Glacial deposit not classified into a specific moraine type.","es":"Depósito glaciar no clasificado en un tipo específico de morrena."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/anillos-o-circulos-de-piedra","prefLabel":{"en":"stone circles","es":"anillos o círculos de piedra"},"definition":{"en":"Circular stone patterns formed by freeze-thaw processes.","es":"Patrones circulares de piedras formados por procesos de hielo-deshielo."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/area-con-cesped-almohadillado","prefLabel":{"en":"tussock area","es":"área con césped almohadillado"},"definition":{"en":"Area with cushion vegetation mounds typical of cold environments.","es":"Zona con montículos de vegetación en cojín típicos de ambientes fríos."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/area-con-suelos-poligonales","prefLabel":{"en":"patterned ground area","es":"área con suelos poligonales"},"definition":{"en":"Area with polygonal soil patterns formed by periglacial processes.","es":"Zona con patrones poligonales en el suelo formados por procesos periglaciales."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/arista","prefLabel":{"en":"arête","es":"arista"},"definition":{"en":"A narrow and sharp ridge between two cirques or glacial valleys.","es":"Cresta estrecha y aguda entre dos circos o valles glaciares."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/bloques-erraticos","prefLabel":{"en":"erratic boulders","es":"bloques erráticos"},"definition":{"en":"Rock boulders transported by a glacier far from their place of origin.","es":"Bloques rocosos transportados por un glaciar lejos de su lugar de origen."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/borde-de-terraza-sobre-depositos-fluvioglaciares","prefLabel":{"en":"fluvioglacial terrace edge","es":"borde de terraza sobre depósitos fluvioglaciares"},"definition":{"en":"Edge of a terrace composed of fluvioglacial deposits.","es":"Borde de una terraza constituida por depósitos fluvioglaciares."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cabecera-de-avalancha-o-alud","prefLabel":{"en":"avalanche starting zone","es":"cabecera de avalancha o alud"},"definition":{"en":"Starting zone of a snow avalanche.","es":"Zona de arranque de una avalancha de nieve."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cabecera-de-avalancha-o-alud-difuso-o-degradado","prefLabel":{"en":"diffuse or degraded avalanche starting zone","es":"cabecera de avalancha o alud difuso o degradado"},"definition":{"en":"Avalanche starting zone with smoothed morphology.","es":"Zona de arranque de avalancha con morfología suavizada."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cambio-de-pendiente-del-valle-glaciar","prefLabel":{"en":"glacial valley slope change","es":"cambio de pendiente del valle glaciar"},"definition":{"en":"Longitudinal slope change in the profile of a glacial valley.","es":"Cambio de pendiente longitudinal en el perfil de un valle glaciar."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/canal-supraglaciar-proglaciar-o-subglaciar","prefLabel":{"en":"supraglacial, proglacial or subglacial channel","es":"canal supraglaciar, proglaciar o subglaciar"},"definition":{"en":"Drainage channel on the surface, front or base of a glacier.","es":"Canal de drenaje en la superficie, frente o base de un glaciar."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/canchal-pedriza-pedrera","prefLabel":{"en":"scree; talus","es":"canchal; pedriza; pedrera"},"definition":{"en":"Accumulation of angular rock fragments at the foot of a wall or scarp.","es":"Acumulación de fragmentos rocosos angulosos al pie de una pared o escarpe."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cavidades","prefLabel":{"en":"cavities","es":"cavidades"},"definition":{"en":"Hollows formed in the ice mass or at its contact with rock.","es":"Oquedades formadas en la masa de hielo o en su contacto con la roca."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/charca-laguna","prefLabel":{"en":"pond; small lake","es":"charca; laguna"},"definition":{"en":"A small body of standing water of glacial origin.","es":"Pequeña masa de agua estancada de origen glaciar."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/circo-glaciar","prefLabel":{"en":"glacial cirque","es":"circo glaciar"},"definition":{"en":"A semicircular amphitheatre-shaped depression excavated by a glacier at the head of a valley.","es":"Depresión semicircular en forma de anfiteatro excavada por un glaciar en la cabecera de un valle."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/circo-glaciar-degradado","prefLabel":{"en":"degraded glacial cirque","es":"circo glaciar degradado"},"definition":{"en":"A glacial cirque whose morphology has been smoothed by subsequent erosional processes.","es":"Circo glaciar cuya morfología ha sido suavizada por procesos erosivos posteriores."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/collado-de-difluencia-glaciar","prefLabel":{"en":"glacial diffluence col","es":"collado de difluencia glaciar"},"definition":{"en":"A pass between two valleys where a glacier overflows into an adjacent valley.","es":"Paso entre dos valles por donde un glaciar desborda hacia un valle adyacente."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/collado-de-transfluencia-glaciar","prefLabel":{"en":"glacial transfluence col","es":"collado de transfluencia glaciar"},"definition":{"en":"A pass where ice from a main glacier flows into an adjacent valley.","es":"Paso por donde el hielo de un glaciar principal fluye hacia un valle adyacente."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cono-de-avalancha-o-alud","prefLabel":{"en":"avalanche cone","es":"cono de avalancha o alud"},"definition":{"en":"Cone-shaped deposit at the base of an avalanche track.","es":"Depósito en forma de cono en la base de un corredor de avalancha."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cono-de-hielo","prefLabel":{"en":"ice cone","es":"cono de hielo"},"definition":{"en":"A conical structure formed by water accumulation and freezing.","es":"Estructura cónica formada por acumulación y congelación de agua."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cono-proglaciar","prefLabel":{"en":"proglacial cone","es":"cono proglaciar"},"definition":{"en":"A cone-shaped deposit formed by glacial meltwater.","es":"Depósito en forma de cono formado por aguas de fusión glaciar."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cordal-o-divisoria-montanyosa","prefLabel":{"en":"mountain ridge","es":"cordal o divisoria montañosa"},"definition":{"en":"A mountain crest that constitutes a watershed divide.","es":"Cresta montañosa que constituye una divisoria de aguas."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cordones-contornos-o-crestas-morrenicas","prefLabel":{"en":"morainic ridges","es":"cordones, contornos o crestas morrénicas"},"definition":{"en":"Elongated ridges formed by morainic accumulation.","es":"Crestas alargadas formadas por acumulación morrénica."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cordones-contornos-o-crestas-morrenicas-difusos-o-degradados","prefLabel":{"en":"diffuse or degraded morainic ridges","es":"cordones, contornos o crestas morrénicas difusos o degradados"},"definition":{"en":"Morainic ridges smoothed by subsequent erosion.","es":"Crestas morrénicas suavizadas por erosión posterior."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cordones-o-contornos-morrenicos-de-nevero","prefLabel":{"en":"snow patch morainic ridges","es":"cordones o contornos morrénicos de nevero"},"definition":{"en":"Morainic ridges formed at the base of a snow patch.","es":"Crestas morrénicas formadas al pie de un nevero."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/corredor-de-avalancha-o-alud","prefLabel":{"en":"avalanche track","es":"corredor de avalancha o alud"},"definition":{"en":"Channel or track along which a snow avalanche descends.","es":"Canal o corredor por donde desciende una avalancha de nieve."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/corredor-rocoso-campo-de-rocas-rio-de-bloques","prefLabel":{"en":"blockstream; block field","es":"corredor rocoso; campo de rocas; río de bloques"},"definition":{"en":"Elongated accumulation of rock blocks descending a slope by periglacial processes.","es":"Acumulación alargada de bloques rocosos que desciende una ladera por procesos periglaciales."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cresta-morrenica-con-indicacion-de-flujo-de-hielo","prefLabel":{"en":"morainic ridge with ice flow indication","es":"cresta morrénica con indicación de flujo de hielo"},"definition":{"en":"Morainic ridge with indication of glacial flow direction.","es":"Cresta morrénica con indicación de la dirección del flujo glaciar."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cubeta-de-sobreexcavacion","prefLabel":{"en":"overdeepened basin","es":"cubeta de sobreexcavación"},"definition":{"en":"A depression excavated by the glacier below the valley equilibrium profile.","es":"Depresión excavada por el glaciar por debajo del perfil de equilibrio del valle."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/deposito-de-opturacion-kame","prefLabel":{"en":"kame deposit","es":"depósito de opturación; kame"},"definition":{"en":"Fluvioglacial deposit accumulated in contact with ice.","es":"Depósito de materiales fluvioglaciares acumulados en contacto con el hielo."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/derrubios-ordenados-o-estratificados-grèzes-litees","prefLabel":{"en":"stratified slope deposits; grèzes litées","es":"derrubios ordenados o estratificados; grèzes litées"},"definition":{"en":"Slope deposits with alternating layers of different grain size of periglacial origin.","es":"Depósitos de ladera con alternancia de capas de diferente granulometría de origen periglaciar."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/direccion-de-flujo-del-hielo","prefLabel":{"en":"ice flow direction","es":"dirección de flujo del hielo"},"definition":{"en":"Indication of the direction of glacier movement.","es":"Indicación de la dirección de movimiento de un glaciar."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/drumlin","prefLabel":{"en":"drumlin","es":"drumlin"},"definition":{"en":"An elongated hill of glacial materials shaped like an inverted spoon, oriented in the ice flow direction.","es":"Colina alargada de materiales glaciares con forma de cuchara invertida, orientada en la dirección del flujo del hielo."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/estrias","prefLabel":{"en":"striations","es":"estrías"},"definition":{"en":"Fine linear marks on rock produced by glacial abrasion.","es":"Marcas lineales finas sobre la roca producidas por abrasión glaciar."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/garganta-subglaciar","prefLabel":{"en":"subglacial gorge","es":"garganta subglaciar"},"definition":{"en":"A gorge excavated by meltwater beneath a glacier.","es":"Garganta excavada por aguas de fusión bajo un glaciar."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/gelifluxion","prefLabel":{"en":"gelifluction","es":"gelifluxión"},"definition":{"en":"Slow flow of saturated soil over a frozen substrate.","es":"Flujo lento del suelo saturado sobre un substrato helado."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/glaciar-de-rocas","prefLabel":{"en":"rock glacier","es":"glaciar de rocas"},"definition":{"en":"A debris mass with interstitial ice that moves slowly downslope.","es":"Masa de derrubios con hielo intersticial que se mueve lentamente ladera abajo."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/glaciar-y-helero","prefLabel":{"en":"glacier and permanent snow field","es":"glaciar y helero"},"definition":{"en":"A mass of ice moving slowly downslope or a permanent snow field.","es":"Masa de hielo que se mueve lentamente ladera abajo o campo de nieve permanente."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/guirnaldas-de-piedras","prefLabel":{"en":"stone garlands","es":"guirnaldas de piedras"},"definition":{"en":"Curved stone alignments on slopes produced by periglacial processes.","es":"Alineaciones curvas de piedras en laderas producidas por procesos periglaciales."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/hidrolacolito","prefLabel":{"en":"hydrolaccolith","es":"hidrolacolito"},"definition":{"en":"A mound formed by freezing of subsurface water that uplifts the surface.","es":"Montículo formado por congelación de agua en el subsuelo que levanta la superficie."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/ladera-con-reptacion-creep","prefLabel":{"en":"slope with creep","es":"ladera con reptación; creep"},"definition":{"en":"A slope affected by slow continuous soil movement due to freeze-thaw cycles.","es":"Vertiente afectada por movimiento lento y continuo del suelo por ciclos de hielo-deshielo."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/lago-de-montanya-ibon","prefLabel":{"en":"mountain lake; tarn","es":"lago de montaña; ibón"},"definition":{"en":"A mountain lake of glacial origin generally located in a cirque.","es":"Lago de montaña de origen glaciar situado generalmente en un circo."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/lago-o-cubeta-colmatada","prefLabel":{"en":"infilled lake or basin","es":"lago o cubeta colmatada"},"definition":{"en":"A glacial lake or basin that has been filled by sediments.","es":"Lago glaciar o cubeta que ha sido rellenada por sedimentos."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/lapiaz-en-hielo","prefLabel":{"en":"ice karren","es":"lapiaz en hielo"},"definition":{"en":"Dissolution or melting forms on ice surface similar to rock karren.","es":"Formas de disolución o fusión en la superficie del hielo similares al lapiaz en roca."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/limite-de-valle-en-artesa","prefLabel":{"en":"U-shaped valley limit","es":"límite de valle en artesa"},"definition":{"en":"Topographic limit of a glacial valley with a U-shaped cross section.","es":"Límite topográfico de un valle glaciar con perfil transversal en U."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/limite-de-valle-en-artesa-degradado","prefLabel":{"en":"degraded U-shaped valley limit","es":"límite de valle en artesa degradado"},"definition":{"en":"Limit of a U-shaped glacial valley smoothed by subsequent erosion.","es":"Límite de un valle glaciar en artesa suavizado por erosión posterior."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/limite-de-zona-glaciada","prefLabel":{"en":"glaciated area limit","es":"límite de zona glaciada"},"definition":{"en":"Limit of the area that was covered by glacial ice.","es":"Límite del área que fue cubierta por hielo glaciar."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/lobulo-de-gelifluxion","prefLabel":{"en":"gelifluction lobe","es":"lóbulo de gelifluxión"},"definition":{"en":"A lobe-shaped form produced by gelifluction on a slope.","es":"Forma lobulada producida por gelifluxión en una ladera."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/lugar-con-rocas-aborregadas","prefLabel":{"en":"roches moutonnées area","es":"lugar con rocas aborregadas"},"definition":{"en":"Area with rock outcrops sculpted by glacial abrasion with asymmetric shape.","es":"Zona con afloramientos rocosos esculpidos por abrasión glaciar con forma asimétrica."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/manto-proglaciar","prefLabel":{"en":"proglacial outwash plain","es":"manto proglaciar"},"definition":{"en":"An extensive flat deposit formed by glacial meltwater.","es":"Depósito extenso y plano formado por aguas de fusión glaciar."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/morrena","prefLabel":{"en":"moraine","es":"morrena"},"definition":{"en":"Accumulation of materials transported and deposited by a glacier.","es":"Acumulación de materiales transportados y depositados por un glaciar."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/morrena-de-fondo","prefLabel":{"en":"ground moraine","es":"morrena de fondo"},"definition":{"en":"Moraine deposited beneath the glacier as a mantle.","es":"Morrena depositada bajo el glaciar en forma de manto."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/morrena-frontal","prefLabel":{"en":"terminal moraine","es":"morrena frontal"},"definition":{"en":"Moraine deposited at the front of a glacier.","es":"Morrena depositada en el frente de un glaciar."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/morrena-lateral-o-central","prefLabel":{"en":"lateral or medial moraine","es":"morrena lateral o central"},"definition":{"en":"Moraine deposited on the flanks or centre of a glacier.","es":"Morrena depositada en los flancos o en el centro de un glaciar."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/morrena-de-nevero","prefLabel":{"en":"snow patch moraine","es":"morrena de nevero"},"definition":{"en":"Moraine associated with a permanent or semi-permanent snow patch.","es":"Morrena asociada a un nevero permanente o semipermanente."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/nicho-o-circo-de-nivacion","prefLabel":{"en":"nivation hollow","es":"nicho o circo de nivación"},"definition":{"en":"A shallow depression formed by nivation processes at the base of a snow patch.","es":"Depresión poco profunda formada por procesos de nivación al pie de un nevero."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/nicho-o-circo-de-nivacion-difuso-o-degradado","prefLabel":{"en":"diffuse or degraded nivation hollow","es":"nicho o circo de nivación difuso o degradado"},"definition":{"en":"A nivation hollow whose shape has been smoothed by subsequent erosion.","es":"Nicho de nivación cuya forma ha sido suavizada por erosión posterior."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/nieve-perpetua","prefLabel":{"en":"permanent snow","es":"nieve perpetua"},"definition":{"en":"Snow accumulation that persists throughout the year.","es":"Acumulación de nieve que persiste durante todo el año."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/pico-principal-aguja-hörn","prefLabel":{"en":"main peak; horn","es":"pico principal, aguja; hörn"},"definition":{"en":"A sharp pyramidal peak sculpted by glacial erosion.","es":"Cima piramidal aguda esculpida por erosión glaciar."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/roca-aborregada","prefLabel":{"en":"roche moutonnée","es":"roca aborregada"},"definition":{"en":"Rock outcrop sculpted by glacial abrasion, polished on the advancing face and plucked on the opposite face.","es":"Afloramiento rocoso esculpido por abrasión glaciar, pulido en la cara de avance y arrancado en la cara opuesta."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/sendas-de-ganado-terracillas-pies-de-vaca","prefLabel":{"en":"cattle tracks; terracettes","es":"sendas de ganado; terracillas; pies de vaca"},"definition":{"en":"Small steps on slopes produced by cattle trampling or creep.","es":"Pequeños escalones en laderas producidos por pisoteo de ganado o reptación."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/seracs-rimayas","prefLabel":{"en":"seracs; bergschrund","es":"seracs; rimayas"},"definition":{"en":"Ice blocks separated by crevasses in steep glacier zones; headwall crevasse.","es":"Bloques de hielo separados por grietas en zonas de fuerte pendiente del glaciar; grieta en la cabecera."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/simas","prefLabel":{"en":"crevasses","es":"simas"},"definition":{"en":"Deep cracks in the ice mass of a glacier.","es":"Grietas profundas en la masa de hielo de un glaciar."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/suelos-estriados","prefLabel":{"en":"striped ground","es":"suelos estriados"},"definition":{"en":"Pattern of alternating bands of coarse and fine material on a slope due to freeze-thaw processes.","es":"Patrón de bandas alternas de material grueso y fino en una ladera por procesos de hielo-deshielo."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/superficie-de-abrasion","prefLabel":{"en":"abrasion surface","es":"superficie de abrasión"},"definition":{"en":"Rock surface polished and striated by glacial abrasion.","es":"Superficie rocosa pulida y estriada por abrasión glaciar."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/superficie-o-rellano-de-crioplanacion","prefLabel":{"en":"cryoplanation surface","es":"superficie o rellano de crioplanación"},"definition":{"en":"Flat surface formed by cryoplanation processes in a periglacial environment.","es":"Superficie plana formada por procesos de crioplanación en ambiente periglaciar."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/talud-o-cono-de-derrubios","prefLabel":{"en":"talus or debris cone","es":"talud o cono de derrubios"},"definition":{"en":"Debris accumulation at the foot of a rock wall forming a cone or talus.","es":"Acumulación de derrubios al pie de una pared rocosa formando un cono o talud."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/terraza-proglaciar","prefLabel":{"en":"proglacial terrace","es":"terraza proglaciar"},"definition":{"en":"A terrace formed by fluvioglacial deposits.","es":"Terraza formada por depósitos fluvioglaciares."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/turbera","prefLabel":{"en":"peat bog","es":"turbera"},"definition":{"en":"Marshy area with accumulation of partially decomposed organic matter (peat).","es":"Zona pantanosa con acumulación de materia orgánica parcialmente descompuesta (turba)."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/turbera-en-ambiente-glaciar-y-periglaciar","prefLabel":{"en":"peat bog","es":"turbera en ambiente lacustra glaciar y periglaciar"},"definition":{"en":"Marshy area with accumulation of partially decomposed organic matter (peat).","es":"Zona pantanosa con acumulación de materia orgánica parcialmente descompuesta (turba)."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/umbral-difuso","prefLabel":{"en":"diffuse threshold","es":"umbral difuso"},"definition":{"en":"A poorly defined rocky step in the floor of a glacial valley.","es":"Resalte rocoso poco marcado en el lecho de un valle glaciar."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/umbral-neto","prefLabel":{"en":"distinct threshold","es":"umbral neto"},"definition":{"en":"A well-defined rocky step in the floor of a glacial valley.","es":"Resalte rocoso bien definido en el lecho de un valle glaciar."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/vertiente-de-bloques","prefLabel":{"en":"block slope","es":"vertiente de bloques"},"definition":{"en":"A slope covered by rock blocks produced by frost shattering.","es":"Vertiente cubierta por bloques rocosos producidos por gelifracción."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/zona-o-superficie-de-pulido-y-abrasion-con-indicacion-de-flujo","prefLabel":{"en":"polished and abraded surface with flow indication","es":"zona o superficie de pulido y abrasión con indicación de flujo"},"definition":{"en":"Glacially polished surface with striations indicating ice flow direction.","es":"Superficie glacialmente pulida con estrías que indican la dirección del flujo del hielo."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/objetos-hidrotermales","prefLabel":{"en":"hydrothermal features","es":"objetos hidrotermales"},"definition":{"en":"Geomorphologic landscapes and landforms related to hydrothermal processes.","es":"Paisajes geomorfológicos y formas del relieve relacionados con procesos hidrotermales."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/objetos-lacustres","prefLabel":{"en":"lacustrine features","es":"objetos lacustres"},"definition":{"en":"Geomorphologic landscapes and landforms related to inland permanent water bodies (lakes).","es":"Paisajes geomorfológicos y formas del relieve relacionados con masas de agua interiores permanentes (lagos)."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/area-endorreica-con-salinizacion-superficial-playa-salina","prefLabel":{"en":"salt flat; saline playa","es":"área endorreica con salinización superficial; playa salina"},"definition":{"en":"An endorheic area with surface salt precipitation.","es":"Área endorréica con precipitación de sales en superficie."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/area-endorreica-playa-encharcamiento-temporal","prefLabel":{"en":"endorheic area; playa","es":"área endorréica; playa; encharcamiento temporal"},"definition":{"en":"An area without external drainage where water accumulates temporarily.","es":"Zona sin drenaje externo donde el agua se acumula temporalmente."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/area-pantanosa","prefLabel":{"en":"marshy area","es":"área pantanosa"},"definition":{"en":"An area with permanently waterlogged soil.","es":"Zona con suelo permanentemente saturado de agua."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/charca-labajo-bodon-estacional","prefLabel":{"en":"seasonal pond","es":"charca; labajo; bodón estacional"},"definition":{"en":"A small seasonal body of standing water.","es":"Pequeña masa de agua estancada de carácter estacional."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/charca-labajo-bodon-permanente","prefLabel":{"en":"permanent pond","es":"charca; labajo; bodón permanente"},"definition":{"en":"A small permanent body of standing water.","es":"Pequeña masa de agua estancada de carácter permanente."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe","prefLabel":{"en":"scarp","es":"escarpe"},"definition":{"en":"An abrupt slope of polygenetic origin.","es":"Talud abrupto de origen poligénico."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe-fosil","prefLabel":{"en":"fossil scarp","es":"escarpe fosil"},"definition":{"en":"A lacustrine scarp no longer in contact with a water body.","es":"Escarpe lacustre que ya no está en contacto con una masa de agua."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpeescarpe-en-ambiente-lacustre","prefLabel":{"en":"scarp","es":"escarpe en ambiente lacustre"},"definition":{"en":"An abrupt slope of polygenetic origin.","es":"Talud abrupto de origen poligénico."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/laguna","prefLabel":{"en":"lagoon; small lake","es":"laguna"},"definition":{"en":"A water body of small extent and shallow depth.","es":"Masa de agua de pequeña extensión y poca profundidad."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/laguna-colmatada-o-desecada","prefLabel":{"en":"infilled or desiccated lagoon","es":"laguna colmatada o desecada"},"definition":{"en":"A lagoon filled with sediments or desiccated.","es":"Laguna rellenada por sedimentos o desecada."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/laguna-estacional","prefLabel":{"en":"seasonal lagoon","es":"laguna estacional"},"definition":{"en":"A lagoon that dries up during certain times of the year.","es":"Laguna que se seca en determinadas épocas del año."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/laguna-permanente","prefLabel":{"en":"permanent lagoon","es":"laguna permanente"},"definition":{"en":"A lagoon with water throughout the year.","es":"Laguna con agua durante todo el año."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/limite-de-cuenca-endorreica","prefLabel":{"en":"endorheic basin limit","es":"límite de cuenca endorréica"},"definition":{"en":"Divide delimiting a basin without drainage to the sea.","es":"Divisoria que delimita una cuenca sin drenaje al mar."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/ojos-de-agua","prefLabel":{"en":"water eyes; springs","es":"ojos de agua"},"definition":{"en":"Point emergences of groundwater.","es":"Surgencias puntuales de agua subterránea."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/reborde-de-terraza-con-indicacion-de-cota-en-metros","prefLabel":{"en":"terrace edge with elevation in metres","es":"reborde de terraza con indicación de cota en metros"},"definition":{"en":"Edge of a lacustrine terrace with elevation indication.","es":"Borde de una terraza lacustre con indicación de su cota."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/terraza-lacustre","prefLabel":{"en":"lacustrine terrace","es":"terraza lacustre"},"definition":{"en":"An elevated flat surface representing a former lake level.","es":"Superficie plana elevada que representa un antiguo nivel de un lago."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/turbera","prefLabel":{"en":"peat bog","es":"turbera"},"definition":{"en":"Marshy area with accumulation of partially decomposed organic matter (peat).","es":"Zona pantanosa con acumulación de materia orgánica parcialmente descompuesta (turba)."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/turbera-en-ambiente-lacustre","prefLabel":{"en":"peat bog","es":"turbera en ambiente lacustre"},"definition":{"en":"Marshy area with accumulation of partially decomposed organic matter (peat).","es":"Zona pantanosa con acumulación de materia orgánica parcialmente descompuesta (turba)."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/objetos-marinos-litorales-y-de-humedales-costeros","prefLabel":{"en":"marine, littoral and coastal wetlands features","es":"objetos marinos, litorales y de humedales costeros"},"definition":{"en":"Geomorphologic landscapes and landforms related to wave or tidal dynamics developed in marine, shallow marine, near-shore and littoral zone environments, and those related to vegetated and / or shallow wet areas","es":"Paisajes geomorfológicos y formas del relieve relativos a la dinámica del oleaje y de las mareas desarrollada en entornos marinos, de aguas poco profundas, cercanos a la costa y litorales, y relativos a humedales con vegetación y poco profundos."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/abanico-de-arena-washover-fan","prefLabel":{"en":"washover fan","es":"abanico de arena; washover fan"},"definition":{"en":"Fan-shaped sand deposit transported by storm waves over a beach ridge.","es":"Depósito en abanico de arena transportada por olas de tormenta sobre un cordón litoral."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/acantilado","prefLabel":{"en":"cliff","es":"acantilado"},"definition":{"en":"A vertical or subvertical coastal scarp carved by marine erosion.","es":"Escarpe vertical o subvertical costero tallado por erosión marina."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/acantilado-entre-25-y-100-metros","prefLabel":{"en":"cliff 25-100 m","es":"acantilado entre 25 y 100 metros"},"definition":{"en":"A coastal cliff between 25 and 100 metres high.","es":"Acantilado costero de entre 25 y 100 metros de altura."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/acantilado-fosil","prefLabel":{"en":"fossil cliff","es":"acantilado fósil"},"definition":{"en":"A relict cliff separated from the current coastline.","es":"Acantilado relicto separado de la línea de costa actual."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/acantilado-inferior-a-25-metros","prefLabel":{"en":"cliff less than 25 m","es":"acantilado inferior a 25 metros"},"definition":{"en":"A coastal cliff less than 25 metres high.","es":"Acantilado costero de menos de 25 metros de altura."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/acantilado-superior-a-100-metros","prefLabel":{"en":"cliff over 100 m","es":"acantilado superior a 100 metros"},"definition":{"en":"A coastal cliff over 100 metres high.","es":"Acantilado costero de más de 100 metros de altura."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/albardon-natural-dique-levee","prefLabel":{"en":"natural levee","es":"albardón natural; dique; levée"},"definition":{"en":"An elongated elevation along the margins of a deltaic channel.","es":"Elevación alargada en las márgenes de un cauce deltaico."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/albufera-laguna-costera-lagoon","prefLabel":{"en":"coastal lagoon","es":"albufera; laguna costera; lagoon"},"definition":{"en":"Shallow water body separated from the sea by a beach ridge.","es":"Masa de agua somera separada del mar por un cordón litoral."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/albufera-colmatada-o-desecada","prefLabel":{"en":"infilled or desiccated coastal lagoon","es":"albufera colmatada o desecada"},"definition":{"en":"A coastal lagoon filled with sediments or desiccated.","es":"Albufera rellenada por sedimentos o desecada."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/banco-barra-fluvial","prefLabel":{"en":"fluvial bank; bar","es":"banco; barra fluvial"},"definition":{"en":"Sediment accumulation in a deltaic river channel.","es":"Acumulación de sedimentos en un cauce fluvial deltaico."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/barra-de-arena","prefLabel":{"en":"sand bar","es":"barra de arena"},"definition":{"en":"An elongated sand accumulation submerged or partially emerged.","es":"Acumulación alargada de arena sumergida o parcialmente emergida."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/barra-sumergida","prefLabel":{"en":"submerged bar","es":"barra sumergida"},"definition":{"en":"An underwater sediment accumulation.","es":"Acumulación de sedimentos bajo el agua."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/boca-de-albufera-grao","prefLabel":{"en":"lagoon inlet","es":"boca de albufera; grao"},"definition":{"en":"Opening connecting a coastal lagoon with the sea.","es":"Abertura de comunicación entre una albufera y el mar."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/borde-de-terraza-con-indicacion-de-cota-en-metros","prefLabel":{"en":"terrace edge with elevation in metres","es":"borde de terraza con indicación de cota en metros"},"definition":{"en":"Edge of a coastal terrace with indication of its elevation above sea level.","es":"Borde de una terraza litoral con indicación de su cota sobre el nivel del mar."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/brazo-fluvial","prefLabel":{"en":"distributary channel","es":"brazo fluvial"},"definition":{"en":"A distribution channel in a delta.","es":"Canal de distribución en un delta."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/brazo-fluvial-abandonado","prefLabel":{"en":"abandoned distributary channel","es":"brazo fluvial abandonado"},"definition":{"en":"A deltaic distribution channel no longer functional.","es":"Canal de distribución deltaico ya no funcional."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/brazo-fluvial-abandonado-inundado-temporalmente","prefLabel":{"en":"temporarily flooded abandoned distributary","es":"brazo fluvial abandonado inundado temporalmente"},"definition":{"en":"An abandoned deltaic channel that is temporarily flooded.","es":"Canal deltaico abandonado que se inunda temporalmente."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/brazo-fluvial-con-flujo-de-marea","prefLabel":{"en":"tidal distributary channel","es":"brazo fluvial con flujo de marea"},"definition":{"en":"A deltaic distribution channel affected by tides.","es":"Canal de distribución deltaico afectado por mareas."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/canal-de-marea","prefLabel":{"en":"tidal channel","es":"canal de marea"},"definition":{"en":"A channel carved by tidal currents.","es":"Canal excavado por las corrientes de marea."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/canal-de-marea-abandonado","prefLabel":{"en":"abandoned tidal channel","es":"canal de marea abandonado"},"definition":{"en":"A tidal channel that is no longer functional.","es":"Canal de marea que ya no es funcional."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/canal-de-marea-sumergido","prefLabel":{"en":"submerged tidal channel","es":"canal de marea sumergido"},"definition":{"en":"A tidal channel permanently underwater.","es":"Canal de marea permanentemente bajo el agua."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/construcciones-biogenicas","prefLabel":{"en":"biogenic constructions","es":"construcciones biogénicas"},"definition":{"en":"Structures built by marine organisms such as coral reefs.","es":"Estructuras construidas por organismos marinos como arrecifes de coral."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cordon-litoral","prefLabel":{"en":"beach ridge; barrier","es":"cordón litoral"},"definition":{"en":"An elongated sediment ridge parallel to the coast.","es":"Cresta alargada de sedimentos paralela a la costa."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/delta","prefLabel":{"en":"delta","es":"delta"},"definition":{"en":"A sedimentary deposit at the mouth of a river.","es":"Depósito sedimentario en la desembocadura de un río."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/delta-sumergido-de-flujo","prefLabel":{"en":"submerged delta; flow delta","es":"delta sumergido; de flujo"},"definition":{"en":"Part of the delta located below water level.","es":"Parte del delta situada bajo el nivel del agua."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/frente-deltaico","prefLabel":{"en":"delta front","es":"frente deltaico"},"definition":{"en":"The frontal zone of a delta in contact with the sea.","es":"Zona frontal de un delta en contacto con el mar."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/llanura-deltaica","prefLabel":{"en":"delta plain","es":"llanura deltaica"},"definition":{"en":"The flat surface of an emerged delta.","es":"Superficie plana de un delta emergido."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/deriva-litoral","prefLabel":{"en":"longshore drift","es":"deriva litoral"},"definition":{"en":"Sediment transport along the coast by longshore currents.","es":"Transporte de sedimentos a lo largo de la costa por corrientes litorales."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/derrame-delta-de-ruptura-de-mota","prefLabel":{"en":"crevasse splay","es":"derrame; delta de ruptura de mota"},"definition":{"en":"Deposit formed by the breach of a natural levee in a delta.","es":"Depósito formado por la rotura del dique natural en un delta."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/direccion-del-viento-dominante","prefLabel":{"en":"prevailing wind direction","es":"dirección del viento dominante"},"definition":{"en":"Predominant wind direction in the coastal area.","es":"Dirección predominante del viento en la zona litoral."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/estuario-marisma","prefLabel":{"en":"estuary; salt marsh","es":"estuario; marisma"},"definition":{"en":"River mouth where fresh and salt water mix.","es":"Desembocadura de un río donde se mezclan aguas dulces y saladas."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/flecha-litoral","prefLabel":{"en":"spit","es":"flecha litoral"},"definition":{"en":"A tongue of sand extending from the coast towards the sea.","es":"Lengua de arena que se extiende desde la costa hacia el mar."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/llanura-de-marea","prefLabel":{"en":"tidal flat","es":"llanura de marea"},"definition":{"en":"A flat surface periodically flooded by tides.","es":"Superficie plana inundada periódicamente por las mareas."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/llanura-de-marea-arenosa","prefLabel":{"en":"sandy tidal flat","es":"llanura de marea arenosa"},"definition":{"en":"A tidal flat with a sandy substrate.","es":"Llanura de marea con substrato arenoso."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/marisma-alta-schorre","prefLabel":{"en":"high marsh; schorre","es":"marisma alta; schorre"},"definition":{"en":"Marsh zone only flooded during spring tides.","es":"Zona de marisma solo inundada en mareas vivas."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/marisma-baja-slikke","prefLabel":{"en":"low marsh; slikke","es":"marisma baja; slikke"},"definition":{"en":"Marsh zone flooded at each tide.","es":"Zona de marisma inundada en cada marea."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/marisma-baja-arenosa","prefLabel":{"en":"sandy low marsh","es":"marisma baja arenosa"},"definition":{"en":"Low marsh with a sandy substrate.","es":"Marisma baja con substrato arenoso."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/plataforma-de-abrasion-rasa","prefLabel":{"en":"wave-cut platform; strandflat","es":"plataforma de abrasión; rasa"},"definition":{"en":"A flat rock surface carved by marine erosion.","es":"Superficie rocosa plana tallada por la erosión marina."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/plataforma-de-abrasion-degradada","prefLabel":{"en":"degraded wave-cut platform","es":"plataforma de abrasión degradada"},"definition":{"en":"A wave-cut platform whose surface has been modified by weathering.","es":"Plataforma de abrasión cuya superficie ha sido modificada por meteorización."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/playa","prefLabel":{"en":"beach","es":"playa"},"definition":{"en":"Sediment accumulation in the coastal zone.","es":"Acumulación de sedimentos en la zona litoral."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/playa-de-arena","prefLabel":{"en":"sand beach","es":"playa de arena"},"definition":{"en":"A beach mainly composed of sand.","es":"Playa constituida principalmente por arena."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/playa-de-cantos-o-bloques","prefLabel":{"en":"pebble or boulder beach","es":"playa de cantos o bloques"},"definition":{"en":"A beach mainly composed of pebbles or boulders.","es":"Playa constituida principalmente por cantos rodados o bloques."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/playa-fangosa","prefLabel":{"en":"muddy beach","es":"playa fangosa"},"definition":{"en":"A beach mainly composed of mud.","es":"Playa constituida principalmente por fango."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/playa-fosil","prefLabel":{"en":"fossil beach","es":"playa fósil"},"definition":{"en":"A relict beach elevated above the current sea level.","es":"Playa relicta elevada respecto al nivel del mar actual."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/surcos-lineas-de-crecimiento-del-cordon-litoral","prefLabel":{"en":"beach ridge growth lines","es":"surcos; líneas de crecimiento del cordón litoral"},"definition":{"en":"Marks indicating the growth phases of a beach ridge.","es":"Marcas que indican las fases de crecimiento de un cordón litoral."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/terraza","prefLabel":{"en":"terrace","es":"terraza"},"definition":{"en":"A flat surface elevated above the current channel, representing a former river level.","es":"Superficie plana elevada respecto al cauce actual, que representa un antiguo nivel del río."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/terraza-erosiva","prefLabel":{"en":"erosional terrace","es":"terraza erosiva"},"definition":{"en":"A terrace carved into rock without significant alluvial deposit.","es":"Terraza tallada en la roca sin depósito aluvial significativo."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/terraza-no-ciclica-de-encajamiento-convergente","prefLabel":{"en":"non-cyclic terrace (entrenching; convergent)","es":"terraza no cíclica (de encajamiento; convergente)"},"definition":{"en":"Terrace formed by progressive entrenchment without relation to climatic cycles.","es":"Terraza formada por encajamiento progresivo sin relación con ciclos climáticos."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/terraza-travertinica","prefLabel":{"en":"travertine terrace","es":"terraza travertínica"},"definition":{"en":"Terrace formed by calcium carbonate (travertine) precipitation.","es":"Terraza formada por precipitación de carbonato cálcico (travertino)."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/terraza-litoral","prefLabel":{"en":"terrace","es":"terraza litoral"},"definition":{"en":"A flat surface elevated above the current channel, representing a former river level.","es":"Superficie plana elevada respecto al cauce actual, que representa un antiguo nivel del río."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/turbera","prefLabel":{"en":"peat bog","es":"turbera"},"definition":{"en":"Marshy area with accumulation of partially decomposed organic matter (peat).","es":"Zona pantanosa con acumulación de materia orgánica parcialmente descompuesta (turba)."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/zona-de-rompiente-zona-intermareal","prefLabel":{"en":"surf zone; intertidal zone","es":"zona de rompiente; zona intermareal"},"definition":{"en":"Coastal strip between high and low tide levels.","es":"Franja litoral entre los niveles de marea alta y baja."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/objetos-relacionados-con-las-laderas-y-con-la-gravedad","prefLabel":{"en":"slope and gravitational features","es":"objetos relacionados con las laderas y con la gravedad"},"definition":{"en":"Geomorphologic landscapes and landforms related to slope environments; geomorphologic landscapes and landforms developed under the action of the gravitational force.","es":"Paisajes geomorfológicos y formas del relieve relacionados con entornos de ladera; paisajes geomorfológicos y formas de relieve desarrollados por efecto de la acción de la gravedad."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/acarcavamiento-embrionario","prefLabel":{"en":"incipient gullying","es":"acarcavamiento embrionario"},"definition":{"en":"Initial phase of gully formation on a slope.","es":"Fase inicial de formación de cárcavas en una vertiente."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/caidas-de-bloques-desprendimientos-derrumbes","prefLabel":{"en":"rockfall; rock collapse","es":"caídas de bloques; desprendimientos; derrumbes"},"definition":{"en":"Detachment of rock blocks from a scarp or wall.","es":"Desprendimiento de bloques rocosos de un escarpe o pared."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cambio-brusco-de-pendiente","prefLabel":{"en":"abrupt slope break","es":"cambio brusco de pendiente"},"definition":{"en":"A sudden change in slope angle on a hillside.","es":"Cambio repentino del ángulo de la pendiente en una vertiente."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/canchal-pedriza","prefLabel":{"en":"scree; block field","es":"canchal; pedriza"},"definition":{"en":"Accumulation of angular rock fragments on a slope.","es":"Acumulación de fragmentos rocosos angulosos en una ladera."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cicatriz-de-despegue-producida-por-movimientos-en-masa","prefLabel":{"en":"mass movement detachment scar","es":"cicatriz de despegue producida por movimientos en masa"},"definition":{"en":"Visible rupture surface at the head zone of a mass movement.","es":"Superficie de rotura visible en la zona de arranque de un movimiento en masa."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/coluvion","prefLabel":{"en":"colluvium","es":"coluvión"},"definition":{"en":"A deposit of loose materials accumulated at the foot of a slope by gravity.","es":"Depósito de materiales sueltos acumulados al pie de una ladera por gravedad."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cono-o-talud-de-derrubios","prefLabel":{"en":"talus cone; scree slope","es":"cono o talud de derrubios"},"definition":{"en":"Accumulation of rock fragments at the foot of a wall or scarp forming a cone or talus.","es":"Acumulación de fragmentos rocosos al pie de una pared o escarpe formando un cono o talud."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/derrubios-ordenados","prefLabel":{"en":"stratified slope deposits","es":"derrubios ordenados"},"definition":{"en":"Slope deposits with some ordering or stratification.","es":"Depósitos de ladera con cierta ordenación o estratificación."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/derrumbe-avalancha","prefLabel":{"en":"rock avalanche","es":"derrumbe; avalancha"},"definition":{"en":"Rapid and massive downslope movement of rocks and debris.","es":"Movimiento rápido y masivo de rocas y derrubios ladera abajo."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/deslizamiento","prefLabel":{"en":"landslide","es":"deslizamiento"},"definition":{"en":"Downslope mass movement of materials along a failure surface.","es":"Movimiento en masa de materiales ladera abajo a lo largo de una superficie de rotura."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/deslizamiento-cartografiable","prefLabel":{"en":"mappable landslide","es":"deslizamiento cartografiable"},"definition":{"en":"A landslide of sufficient dimensions to be represented on a map.","es":"Deslizamiento de dimensiones suficientes para ser representado en un mapa."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/facetas-triangulares-de-vertiente","prefLabel":{"en":"triangular slope facets","es":"facetas triangulares de vertiente"},"definition":{"en":"Triangular surfaces on slopes produced by the intersection of transverse valleys.","es":"Superficies triangulares en vertientes producidas por la intersección de valles transversales."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/flujo","prefLabel":{"en":"flow","es":"flujo"},"definition":{"en":"A mass movement with viscous fluid behavior.","es":"Movimiento en masa con comportamiento de fluido viscoso."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/ladera-con-reptacion","prefLabel":{"en":"slope with creep","es":"ladera con reptación"},"definition":{"en":"A slope affected by slow and continuous movement of soil or regolith.","es":"Vertiente afectada por movimiento lento y continuo del suelo o regolito."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/lajamiento-sheeting","prefLabel":{"en":"sheeting","es":"lajamiento; sheeting"},"definition":{"en":"Rock fracturing into sheets parallel to the topographic surface.","es":"Fracturación de la roca en láminas paralelas a la superficie topográfica."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/lobulo-o-colada-de-solifluxion","prefLabel":{"en":"solifluction lobe","es":"lóbulo o colada de solifluxión"},"definition":{"en":"A lobe-shaped form produced by solifluction on a slope.","es":"Forma lobulada producida por solifluxión en una ladera."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/terracillas","prefLabel":{"en":"terracettes","es":"terracillas"},"definition":{"en":"Small steps parallel to contour lines on a slope, produced by creep or trampling.","es":"Pequeños escalones paralelos a las curvas de nivel en una ladera, producidos por reptación o pisoteo."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/vertiente-con-bloques","prefLabel":{"en":"block-covered slope","es":"vertiente con bloques"},"definition":{"en":"A slope covered by rock blocks from the upper part.","es":"Vertiente cubierta por bloques rocosos procedentes de la parte superior."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/vertiente-con-surcos-de-erosion-rills","prefLabel":{"en":"slope with rills","es":"vertiente con surcos de erosión (rills)"},"definition":{"en":"A slope with small linear grooves formed by surface runoff.","es":"Vertiente con pequeños surcos lineales formados por escorrentía superficial."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/vertiente-regularizada","prefLabel":{"en":"regularized slope","es":"vertiente regularizada"},"definition":{"en":"A slope whose profile has been smoothed by erosion and sedimentation processes.","es":"Vertiente cuyo perfil ha sido suavizado por procesos de erosión y sedimentación."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/vertiente-regularizada-y-disectada","prefLabel":{"en":"regularized and dissected slope","es":"vertiente regularizada y disectada"},"definition":{"en":"A regularized slope that has been subsequently incised by channels.","es":"Vertiente regularizada que ha sido posteriormente incidida por cauces."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/zona-con-solifluxion","prefLabel":{"en":"solifluction zone","es":"zona con solifluxión"},"definition":{"en":"Area affected by slow flow of saturated soil over a frozen or impermeable substrate.","es":"Área afectada por flujo lento del suelo saturado sobre un substrato helado o impermeable."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/objetos-tectonicos-y-estructurales","prefLabel":{"en":"tectonic and structural features","es":"objetos tectónicos y estructurales"},"definition":{"en":"Geomorphologic landscapes and landforms related to regional or local bedrock structures, or crustal movement; and geomorphologic landscapes and landforms related dominantly to water erosion but excluding perennial, channel flow (i.e. fluvial, glaciofluvial), or eolian erosion.","es":"Paisajes geomorfológicos y formas del relieve resultantes de estructuras regionales o locales de roca o de movimientos tectónicos o corticales; asimismo, paisajes geomorfológicos y formas de relieve de origen tectónico o exhumados predominantemente por la erosión del agua, con exclusión de las corrientes canalizadas perennes (es decir, fluviales o glaciofluviales), o por la erosión eólica."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/alineacion-morfologica-con-control-estructural","prefLabel":{"en":"structurally controlled morphological alignment","es":"alineación morfológica con control estructural"},"definition":{"en":"Alignment of relief forms controlled by the underlying geological structure.","es":"Alineación de formas del relieve controlada por la estructura geológica subyacente."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/basculamiento","prefLabel":{"en":"tilting","es":"basculamiento"},"definition":{"en":"Inclination of a block or surface due to tectonic movements.","es":"Inclinación de un bloque o superficie por movimientos tectónicos."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cerro-conico","prefLabel":{"en":"conical hill","es":"cerro cónico"},"definition":{"en":"A conical terrain elevation.","es":"Elevación del terreno de forma cónica."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cresta-barra","prefLabel":{"en":"ridge; bar","es":"cresta; barra"},"definition":{"en":"Elongated and narrow positive relief controlled by resistant layers.","es":"Relieve positivo alargado y estrecho controlado por capas resistentes."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe-de-contacto-diapirico","prefLabel":{"en":"diapiric contact scarp","es":"escarpe de contacto diapírico"},"definition":{"en":"A topographic scarp formed at the contact of a diapiric body with adjacent rocks.","es":"Escarpe topográfico originado en el contacto de un cuerpo diapírico con las rocas adyacentes."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe-de-contacto-intrusivo","prefLabel":{"en":"intrusive contact scarp","es":"escarpe de contacto intrusivo"},"definition":{"en":"A topographic scarp formed at the contact between an intrusive rock and the host rock.","es":"Escarpe topográfico originado en el contacto entre una roca intrusiva y la roca encajante."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe-de-linea-de-falla","prefLabel":{"en":"fault-line scarp","es":"escarpe de línea de falla"},"definition":{"en":"A topographic scarp coinciding with the trace of a fault.","es":"Escarpe topográfico coincidente con el trazado de una falla."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe-de-linea-de-falla-degradado","prefLabel":{"en":"degraded fault-line scarp","es":"escarpe de línea de falla degradado"},"definition":{"en":"A fault-line scarp whose morphology has been smoothed by erosional processes.","es":"Escarpe de falla cuya morfología ha sido suavizada por procesos erosivos."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe-de-linea-de-falla-en-retroceso","prefLabel":{"en":"retreating fault-line scarp","es":"escarpe de línea de falla en retroceso"},"definition":{"en":"A fault-line scarp whose position progressively shifts due to erosional retreat.","es":"Escarpe de falla cuya posición se desplaza progresivamente por retroceso erosivo."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe-de-linea-de-falla-exhumado","prefLabel":{"en":"exhumed fault-line scarp","es":"escarpe de línea de falla exhumado"},"definition":{"en":"A fault-line scarp re-exposed after having been covered by younger materials.","es":"Escarpe de falla que ha sido re-expuesto tras haber estado cubierto por materiales más recientes."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe-de-linea-de-falla-inversa-o-cabalgamiento","prefLabel":{"en":"reverse or thrust fault-line scarp","es":"escarpe de línea de falla inversa o cabalgamiento"},"definition":{"en":"A topographic scarp associated with a reverse or thrust fault.","es":"Escarpe topográfico asociado a una falla inversa o cabalgamiento."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe-de-linea-de-falla-originado-por-erosion-diferencial","prefLabel":{"en":"differential erosion fault-line scarp","es":"escarpe de línea de falla originado por erosión diferencial"},"definition":{"en":"A scarp resulting from differential erosion along a fault line.","es":"Escarpe resultante de la erosión diferencial a lo largo de una línea de falla."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe-estructural","prefLabel":{"en":"structural scarp","es":"escarpe estructural"},"definition":{"en":"A topographic scarp controlled by the arrangement of geological layers.","es":"Escarpe topográfico controlado por la disposición de las capas geológicas."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe-estructural-en-capas-horizontales-entre-25-100-metros","prefLabel":{"en":"structural scarp in horizontal layers (25-100 m)","es":"escarpe estructural en capas horizontales (entre 25-100 metros)"},"definition":{"en":"A scarp 25 to 100 m high in horizontal layers.","es":"Escarpe de 25 a 100 m de altura en capas horizontales."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe-estructural-en-capas-horizontales-inferior-a-25-metros","prefLabel":{"en":"structural scarp in horizontal layers (<25 m)","es":"escarpe estructural en capas horizontales (inferior a 25 metros)"},"definition":{"en":"A scarp less than 25 m high in horizontal layers.","es":"Escarpe de menos de 25 m de altura en capas horizontales."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe-estructural-en-capas-horizontales-superior-a-100-metros","prefLabel":{"en":"structural scarp in horizontal layers (>100 m)","es":"escarpe estructural en capas horizontales (superior a 100 metros)"},"definition":{"en":"A scarp over 100 m high in horizontal layers.","es":"Escarpe de más de 100 m de altura en capas horizontales."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe-estructural-en-capas-monoclinales-entre-25-100-metros-cuesta","prefLabel":{"en":"cuesta scarp (25-100 m)","es":"escarpe estructural en capas monoclinales (entre 25-100 metros); cuesta"},"definition":{"en":"A scarp 25 to 100 m in monoclinal layers forming a cuesta.","es":"Escarpe de 25 a 100 m en capas monoclinales formando una cuesta."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe-estructural-en-capas-monoclinales-inferior-a-25-metros-cuesta","prefLabel":{"en":"cuesta scarp (<25 m)","es":"escarpe estructural en capas monoclinales (inferior a 25 metros); cuesta"},"definition":{"en":"A scarp less than 25 m in monoclinal layers forming a cuesta.","es":"Escarpe de menos de 25 m en capas monoclinales formando una cuesta."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe-estructural-en-capas-monoclinales-superior-a-100-metros-cuesta","prefLabel":{"en":"cuesta scarp (>100 m)","es":"escarpe estructural en capas monoclinales (superior a 100 metros); cuesta"},"definition":{"en":"A scarp over 100 m in monoclinal layers forming a cuesta.","es":"Escarpe de más de 100 m en capas monoclinales formando una cuesta."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/facetas-triangulares-de-escarpe-de-falla","prefLabel":{"en":"triangular facets of fault scarp","es":"facetas triangulares de escarpe de falla"},"definition":{"en":"Triangular surfaces on the slope of a fault scarp produced by the intersection of transverse valleys.","es":"Superficies triangulares en la ladera de un escarpe de falla producidas por la intersección de valles transversales."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/falla","prefLabel":{"en":"fault","es":"falla"},"definition":{"en":"A fracture or zone of fractures along which there has been displacement of the adjacent blocks.","es":"Fractura o zona de fractura a lo largo de la cual ha habido desplazamiento de los bloques contiguos."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/falla-en-direccion-desgarre","prefLabel":{"en":"strike-slip fault","es":"falla en dirección; desgarre"},"definition":{"en":"A fault in which the displacement is predominantly horizontal and parallel to the strike of the fault.","es":"Falla en la que el desplazamiento es predominantemente horizontal y paralelo al rumbo de la falla."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/falla-inversa-frente-de-cabalgamiento","prefLabel":{"en":"reverse fault; thrust front","es":"falla inversa; frente de cabalgamiento"},"definition":{"en":"A fault in which the hanging wall has moved upward relative to the footwall; when the angle is low it is called a thrust.","es":"Falla en la que el bloque superior se ha desplazado hacia arriba respecto al bloque inferior; cuando el ángulo es bajo se denomina cabalgamiento."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/falla-normal-con-indicacion-de-labio-hundido","prefLabel":{"en":"normal fault with downthrown side indication","es":"falla normal con indicación de labio hundido"},"definition":{"en":"A fault in which the hanging wall has moved downward relative to the footwall, with indication of the downthrown side.","es":"Falla en la que el bloque superior se ha desplazado hacia abajo respecto al bloque inferior, con indicación del labio hundido."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/falla-supuesta","prefLabel":{"en":"inferred fault","es":"falla supuesta"},"definition":{"en":"A fault whose existence is inferred from indirect evidence but has not been directly observed.","es":"Falla cuya existencia se deduce de evidencias indirectas pero no se ha observado directamente."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/flexion-monoclinal","prefLabel":{"en":"monoclinal flexure","es":"flexión monoclinal"},"definition":{"en":"An inflection or change in dip in layers forming a monoclinal relief.","es":"Inflexión o cambio de buzamiento en capas que forman un relieve monoclinal."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/frente-montanyoso-lineal","prefLabel":{"en":"linear mountain front","es":"frente montañoso lineal"},"definition":{"en":"A mountain front with a rectilinear trace controlled by a fault or tectonic structure.","es":"Frente montañoso de trazado rectilíneo controlado por una falla o estructura tectónica."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/linea-de-capa-con-indicacion-de-buzamiento","prefLabel":{"en":"bedding trace with dip indication","es":"línea de capa con indicación de buzamiento"},"definition":{"en":"Trace of a sedimentary bed at the surface with indication of the dip angle.","es":"Traza de una capa sedimentaria en superficie con indicación del ángulo de buzamiento."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/relieve-conforme-anticlinal-mont","prefLabel":{"en":"anticlinal conform relief; mont","es":"relieve conforme anticlinal; mont"},"definition":{"en":"Positive relief whose morphology coincides with the shape of an underlying anticline.","es":"Relieve positivo cuya morfología coincide con la forma de un anticlinal subyacente."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/relieve-conforme-sinclinal-val","prefLabel":{"en":"synclinal conform relief; val","es":"relieve conforme sinclinal; val"},"definition":{"en":"Negative relief whose morphology coincides with the shape of an underlying syncline.","es":"Relieve negativo cuya morfología coincide con la forma de un sinclinal subyacente."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/relieve-invertido","prefLabel":{"en":"inverted relief","es":"relieve invertido"},"definition":{"en":"Relief in which the topographic forms are opposite to the underlying geological structure.","es":"Relieve en el que las formas topográficas son opuestas a la estructura geológica subyacente."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/resalte-de-capas-subverticales","prefLabel":{"en":"ledge of subvertical layers","es":"resalte de capas subverticales"},"definition":{"en":"A rock ledge formed by resistant subvertical layers.","es":"Saliente rocoso formado por capas subverticales resistentes."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/resalte-de-diques","prefLabel":{"en":"dyke ridge","es":"resalte de diques"},"definition":{"en":"A topographic ridge caused by differential erosion of a resistant volcanic dyke.","es":"Resalte topográfico causado por erosión diferencial de un dique volcánico resistente."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/resalte-en-capas-horizontales","prefLabel":{"en":"ledge in horizontal layers","es":"resalte en capas horizontales"},"definition":{"en":"A rock ledge in horizontal layers forming a step in the topography.","es":"Saliente rocoso en capas horizontales que forma un escalón en la topografía."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/resalte-en-capas-inclinadas-chevrons","prefLabel":{"en":"inclined layer ledge; chevrons","es":"resalte en capas inclinadas; chevrons"},"definition":{"en":"A topographic ledge in inclined layers displaying V-shapes or chevron patterns.","es":"Resalte topográfico en capas inclinadas que presenta formas en V o chevron."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/rumbo-e-inclinacion-o-buzamiento","prefLabel":{"en":"strike and dip","es":"rumbo e inclinación o buzamiento"},"definition":{"en":"Representation of the orientation of a bed or planar structure by its strike and dip.","es":"Representación de la orientación de una capa o estructura planar mediante su rumbo y buzamiento."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/superficie-estructural-degradada","prefLabel":{"en":"degraded structural surface","es":"superficie estructural degradada"},"definition":{"en":"A structural surface whose original form has been modified by erosional processes.","es":"Superficie estructural cuya forma original ha sido modificada por procesos erosivos."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/superficie-estructural-exhumada","prefLabel":{"en":"exhumed structural surface","es":"superficie estructural (exhumada)"},"definition":{"en":"A resistant stratum surface exposed by erosion of overlying materials.","es":"Superficie de un estrato resistente expuesta por erosión de los materiales suprayacentes."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/superficie-subestructural-terminal","prefLabel":{"en":"substructural surface","es":"superficie subestructural (terminal)"},"definition":{"en":"An erosional surface developed close to and subparallel to an underlying resistant stratum.","es":"Superficie erosiva desarrollada próxima y subparalela a un estrato resistente subyacente."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/valle-de-fractura","prefLabel":{"en":"fracture valley","es":"valle de fractura"},"definition":{"en":"A valley carved along a fracture zone or fault.","es":"Valle excavado a favor de una zona de fractura o falla."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/zona-intensamente-fracturada","prefLabel":{"en":"intensely fractured zone","es":"zona intensamente fracturada"},"definition":{"en":"A zone with a very high density of fractures that conditions the terrain morphology.","es":"Zona con una densidad muy elevada de fracturas que condiciona la morfología del terreno."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/objetos-volcanicos","prefLabel":{"en":"volcanic features","es":"objetos volcánicos"},"definition":{"en":"Geomorphologic landscapes and landforms related to the deep seated (igneous) processes by which magma and associated gases rise through the crust and are extruded onto the earth's surface and into the atmosphere.","es":"Paisajes geomorfológicos y formas del relieve relativos a procesos ígneos en virtud de los cuales magma y gases asociados atraviesan la corteza y son expulsados sobre la superficie terrestre y a la atmósfera."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/bombas-bloques-erraticos","prefLabel":{"en":"volcanic bombs; erratic blocks","es":"bombas; bloques erráticos"},"definition":{"en":"Large lava fragments expelled during a volcanic eruption.","es":"Fragmentos de lava de gran tamaño expulsados durante una erupción volcánica."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/borde-de-caldera","prefLabel":{"en":"caldera rim","es":"borde de caldera"},"definition":{"en":"The topographic rim that delimits a volcanic caldera.","es":"Borde topográfico que delimita una caldera volcánica."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/borde-de-caldera-degradado","prefLabel":{"en":"degraded caldera rim","es":"borde de caldera degradado"},"definition":{"en":"A volcanic caldera rim partially destroyed by erosion.","es":"Borde de caldera volcánica parcialmente destruido por erosión."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/borde-de-crater-de-explosion-hidro-magmatica-con-anillo-de-toba-conservado","prefLabel":{"en":"hydromagmatic explosion crater rim with preserved tuff ring","es":"borde de cráter de explosión hidro-magmática con anillo de toba conservado"},"definition":{"en":"Maar crater rim with a preserved ring of pyroclastic tuffs.","es":"Borde de cráter de maar con anillo de tobas piroclásticas conservado."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/campo-de-cenizas","prefLabel":{"en":"ash field","es":"campo de cenizas"},"definition":{"en":"An area covered by volcanic ash.","es":"Zona cubierta por cenizas volcánicas."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/centro-de-emision","prefLabel":{"en":"emission centre","es":"centro de emisión"},"definition":{"en":"A point or zone from which volcanic material is emitted.","es":"Punto o zona desde donde se produce la emisión de material volcánico."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/chimenea","prefLabel":{"en":"volcanic chimney","es":"chimenea"},"definition":{"en":"A vertical conduit through which magma rises to the surface.","es":"Conducto vertical por el que asciende el magma hasta la superficie."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cicatriz-de-deslizamiento-inducido-por-actividad-volcanica","prefLabel":{"en":"volcano-induced landslide scar","es":"cicatriz de deslizamiento inducido por actividad volcánica"},"definition":{"en":"Scar of a landslide caused by volcanic activity.","es":"Cicatriz de un deslizamiento provocado por actividad volcánica."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/colada-de-lava","prefLabel":{"en":"lava flow","es":"colada de lava"},"definition":{"en":"A mass of lava that flows or has flowed over the ground surface.","es":"Masa de lava que fluye o ha fluido sobre la superficie del terreno."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/colada-de-lava-lineal-salideros-lavicos","prefLabel":{"en":"linear lava flow; lava outbreak","es":"colada de lava lineal; salideros lávicos"},"definition":{"en":"A lava flow with linear morphology or lateral lava outbreak.","es":"Colada de lava de morfología lineal o salida lateral de lava."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/colada-de-lava-tipo-aa-con-bloques-y-escorias-malpais","prefLabel":{"en":"aa lava flow; malpais","es":"colada de lava tipo aa; con bloques y escorias; malpaís"},"definition":{"en":"A lava flow with a rough surface of blocks and scoriae.","es":"Colada de lava de superficie rugosa con bloques y escorias."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/colada-de-lava-tipo-pahoehoe-lava-cordada","prefLabel":{"en":"pahoehoe lava flow; ropy lava","es":"colada de lava tipo pahoehoe; lava cordada"},"definition":{"en":"A lava flow with a smooth surface and ropy morphology.","es":"Colada de lava de superficie lisa con morfología cordada."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/colada-masiva-con-superficie-lisa","prefLabel":{"en":"massive lava flow with smooth surface","es":"colada masiva con superficie lisa"},"definition":{"en":"A compact lava flow with a smooth and homogeneous surface.","es":"Colada de lava compacta con superficie lisa y homogénea."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/colada-meteorizada-o-degradada","prefLabel":{"en":"weathered or degraded lava flow","es":"colada meteorizada o degradada"},"definition":{"en":"A lava flow whose surface has been altered by weathering.","es":"Colada de lava cuya superficie ha sido alterada por meteorización."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cono-de-piroclastos","prefLabel":{"en":"pyroclastic cone","es":"cono de piroclastos"},"definition":{"en":"A volcanic edifice formed by accumulation of pyroclastic material around an emission centre.","es":"Edificio volcánico formado por acumulación de piroclastos alrededor de un centro de emisión."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cono-de-piroclastos-alomado-cabezo","prefLabel":{"en":"rounded pyroclastic cone","es":"cono de piroclastos alomado; cabezo"},"definition":{"en":"A pyroclastic cone with a rounded shape due to advanced degradation.","es":"Cono de piroclastos con forma redondeada por degradación avanzada."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cono-de-piroclastos-degradado-con-centro-de-emision","prefLabel":{"en":"degraded pyroclastic cone with emission centre","es":"cono de piroclastos degradado con centro de emisión"},"definition":{"en":"A pyroclastic cone whose morphology has been degraded by erosion, preserving the emission centre.","es":"Cono de piroclastos cuya morfología ha sido degradada por erosión, conservando el centro de emisión."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cono-volcanico-con-crater","prefLabel":{"en":"volcanic cone with crater","es":"cono volcánico con cráter"},"definition":{"en":"A conical volcanic edifice that preserves its summit crater.","es":"Edificio volcánico cónico que conserva su cráter en la cima."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/crater","prefLabel":{"en":"crater","es":"cráter"},"definition":{"en":"A circular or subcircular depression at the summit of a volcanic edifice.","es":"Depresión circular o subcircular en la cima de un edificio volcánico."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/crater-activo","prefLabel":{"en":"active crater","es":"cráter activo"},"definition":{"en":"A volcanic crater with current fumarolic, seismic or eruptive activity.","es":"Cráter volcánico con actividad fumarólica, sísmica o eruptiva actual."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/crater-con-lago","prefLabel":{"en":"crater lake","es":"cráter con lago"},"definition":{"en":"A volcanic crater containing a lake.","es":"Cráter volcánico que contiene un lago."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/crater-inactivo","prefLabel":{"en":"inactive crater","es":"cráter inactivo"},"definition":{"en":"A volcanic crater without current activity.","es":"Cráter volcánico sin actividad actual."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/crater-de-domo-colada","prefLabel":{"en":"dome-flow crater","es":"cráter de domo-colada"},"definition":{"en":"A crater associated with a volcanic dome and its associated flows.","es":"Cráter asociado a un domo volcánico y sus coladas asociadas."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/crater-de-explosion","prefLabel":{"en":"explosion crater","es":"cráter de explosión"},"definition":{"en":"A circular or subcircular depression produced by a volcanic explosion.","es":"Depresión circular o subcircular producida por una explosión volcánica."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/depresion-intralavica","prefLabel":{"en":"intralava depression","es":"depresión intralávica"},"definition":{"en":"A depression formed within a lava flow by collapse or deflation.","es":"Depresión formada dentro de una colada de lava por colapso o deflación."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/direccion-de-flujo-de-lava","prefLabel":{"en":"lava flow direction","es":"dirección de flujo de lava"},"definition":{"en":"Indication of the direction of movement of a lava flow.","es":"Indicación de la dirección de movimiento de una colada de lava."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/disyuncion-columnar","prefLabel":{"en":"columnar jointing","es":"disyunción columnar"},"definition":{"en":"Prismatic columnar fracturing of volcanic rocks due to cooling.","es":"Fracturación en columnas prismáticas de rocas volcánicas por enfriamiento."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/domo","prefLabel":{"en":"dome","es":"domo"},"definition":{"en":"A rounded elevation formed by extrusion of viscous lava.","es":"Elevación redondeada formada por extrusión de lava viscosa."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/domo-endogeno","prefLabel":{"en":"endogenous dome","es":"domo endógeno"},"definition":{"en":"A volcanic dome formed by magma injection that uplifts surface layers.","es":"Domo volcánico formado por inyección de magma que levanta las capas superficiales."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/domo-exogeno","prefLabel":{"en":"exogenous dome","es":"domo exógeno"},"definition":{"en":"A volcanic dome formed by lava extrusion at the surface.","es":"Domo volcánico formado por extrusión de lava en superficie."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/domo-volcanico","prefLabel":{"en":"dome","es":"domo volcánico"},"definition":{"en":"A rounded elevation formed by extrusion of viscous lava.","es":"Elevación redondeada formada por extrusión de lava viscosa."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe-frente-de-colada","prefLabel":{"en":"scarp; lava flow front","es":"escarpe; frente de colada"},"definition":{"en":"The front or abrupt edge of a lava flow.","es":"Frente o borde abrupto de una colada de lava."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/fisura","prefLabel":{"en":"fissure","es":"fisura"},"definition":{"en":"An open fracture in a volcanic edifice through which lava or gases may be emitted.","es":"Fractura abierta en un edificio volcánico por la que puede producirse emisión de lava o gases."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/fisura-con-fumarola-emergente","prefLabel":{"en":"fissure with active fumarole","es":"fisura con fumarola emergente"},"definition":{"en":"A volcanic fracture with active gas and steam emission.","es":"Fractura volcánica con emisión activa de gases y vapor."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/fuente-termal","prefLabel":{"en":"thermal spring","es":"fuente termal"},"definition":{"en":"A spring of water heated by geothermal activity.","es":"Manantial de agua calentada por actividad geotérmica."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/geiser","prefLabel":{"en":"geyser","es":"geiser"},"definition":{"en":"A thermal spring that periodically emits jets of hot water and steam.","es":"Fuente termal que emite periódicamente chorros de agua caliente y vapor."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/gruta-jameo","prefLabel":{"en":"grotto; jameo","es":"gruta; jameo"},"definition":{"en":"A cavity of volcanic origin, frequently associated with a collapsed lava tube.","es":"Cavidad de origen volcánico, frecuentemente asociada a un tubo de lava colapsado."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/hornito","prefLabel":{"en":"hornito","es":"hornito"},"definition":{"en":"A small mound of ejected lava formed on a flow.","es":"Pequeño montículo de lava proyectada formado sobre una colada."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/hundimiento-subsidencia","prefLabel":{"en":"collapse; subsidence","es":"hundimiento; subsidencia"},"definition":{"en":"Ground lowering by collapse or subsidence of volcanic origin.","es":"Descenso del terreno por colapso o subsidencia de origen volcánico."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/meteorizacion-fumarolica","prefLabel":{"en":"fumarolic weathering","es":"meteorización fumarólica"},"definition":{"en":"Alteration of volcanic rock by fumarolic gas action.","es":"Alteración de la roca volcánica por acción de gases fumarólicos."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/muro-o-dique-lateral-de-enfriamiento-levee","prefLabel":{"en":"lateral cooling levee","es":"muro o dique lateral de enfriamiento; levée"},"definition":{"en":"A lateral dyke formed by cooling of the edge of a lava flow.","es":"Dique lateral formado por enfriamiento del borde de una colada de lava."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/ojivas-de-presion","prefLabel":{"en":"pressure ridges","es":"ojivas de presión"},"definition":{"en":"Arched ridges on a lava flow surface caused by internal pressure.","es":"Crestas arqueadas en la superficie de una colada de lava causadas por presión interna."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/piton-aguja-necks","prefLabel":{"en":"volcanic plug; neck","es":"pitón; aguja; necks"},"definition":{"en":"A mass of solidified lava in the volcanic chimney exposed by erosion.","es":"Masa de lava solidificada en el interior de la chimenea volcánica expuesta por erosión."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/resalte-de-diques","prefLabel":{"en":"dyke ridge","es":"resalte de diques"},"definition":{"en":"A topographic ridge caused by differential erosion of a resistant volcanic dyke.","es":"Resalte topográfico causado por erosión diferencial de un dique volcánico resistente."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/resalte-de-diques-volcanico","prefLabel":{"en":"dyke ridge","es":"resalte de diques volcánico"},"definition":{"en":"A topographic ridge caused by differential erosion of a resistant volcanic dyke.","es":"Resalte topográfico causado por erosión diferencial de un dique volcánico resistente."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/ruptura-de-pendiente-cascada-en-colada","prefLabel":{"en":"slope break; lava cascade","es":"ruptura de pendiente; cascada en colada"},"definition":{"en":"An abrupt slope change in a lava flow.","es":"Cambio brusco de pendiente en una colada de lava."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/ruptura-de-pendiente-debido-a-reflejos-de-antiguos-bordes-de-crateres","prefLabel":{"en":"slope break due to ancient crater rim remnants","es":"ruptura de pendiente debido a reflejos de antiguos bordes de cráteres"},"definition":{"en":"Slope change associated with remnants of ancient volcanic crater rims.","es":"Cambio de pendiente asociado a restos de antiguos bordes de cráteres volcánicos."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/superficie-de-apilamiento-con-indicacion-de-inclinacion-de-la-misma","prefLabel":{"en":"stacking surface with dip indication","es":"superficie de apilamiento con indicación de inclinación de la misma"},"definition":{"en":"Contact surface between stacked lava flows or volcanic units with dip indication.","es":"Superficie de contacto entre coladas o unidades volcánicas apiladas con indicación de su inclinación."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/surgencia-lavica-bajo-colada-solidificada","prefLabel":{"en":"lava upwelling beneath solidified flow","es":"surgencia lávica bajo colada solidificada"},"definition":{"en":"Fluid lava emerging beneath the solidified crust of a flow.","es":"Salida de lava fluida bajo la costra solidificada de una colada."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/trazas-resaltes-de-capas-en-apilamientos-volcanicos-inclinados","prefLabel":{"en":"layer traces in inclined volcanic stacks","es":"trazas, resaltes de capas en apilamientos volcánicos inclinados"},"definition":{"en":"Topographic ledges of layers in inclined volcanic sequences.","es":"Resaltes topográficos de capas en secuencias volcánicas inclinadas."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/trazas-resaltes-de-capas-en-apilamientos-volcanicos-subhorizontales","prefLabel":{"en":"layer traces in subhorizontal volcanic stacks","es":"trazas, resaltes de capas en apilamientos volcánicos subhorizontales"},"definition":{"en":"Topographic ledges of layers in subhorizontal volcanic sequences.","es":"Resaltes topográficos de capas en secuencias volcánicas subhorizontales."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/tunel-de-lava","prefLabel":{"en":"lava tube","es":"túnel de lava"},"definition":{"en":"An underground conduit formed by lava flowing beneath a solidified crust.","es":"Conducto subterráneo formado por el flujo de lava bajo una costra solidificada."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/volcan-de-barro","prefLabel":{"en":"mud volcano","es":"volcán de barro"},"definition":{"en":"A structure formed by the emission of mud, water and gases at the surface.","es":"Estructura formada por emisión de barro, agua y gases a la superficie."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/volcan-de-barro-con-deposito-fangoso","prefLabel":{"en":"mud volcano with mud deposit","es":"volcán de barro con depósito fangoso"},"definition":{"en":"A mud volcano with visible accumulation of muddy deposits.","es":"Volcán de barro con acumulación visible de depósitos fangosos."}}]}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/superficie-de-erosion","prefLabel":{"en":"erosion surface","es":"superficie de erosión"},"definition":{"en":"Geomorphologic landscapes and landforms related dominantly to water erosion but excluding perennial channel flow (i.e. fluvial, glaciofluvial) or eolian erosion.","es":"Paisajes geomorfológicos y formas del relieve relacionados predominantemente con la erosión del agua, con exclusión de las corrientes canalizadas perennes (es decir, fluviales, glaciofluviales), o a la erosión eólica."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cerro-conico","prefLabel":{"en":"conical hill","es":"cerro cónico"},"definition":{"en":"A conical terrain elevation.","es":"Elevación del terreno de forma cónica."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cerro-conico-poligenetico","prefLabel":{"en":"conical hill","es":"cerro cónico poligenético"},"definition":{"en":"A conical terrain elevation.","es":"Elevación del terreno de forma cónica."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cerro-ruiniforme-caos-de-bloques","prefLabel":{"en":"ruiniform hill; block chaos","es":"cerro ruiniforme poligenetico"},"altLabel":{"es":["caos de bloques"]},"definition":{"en":"Relief with a ruin-like appearance due to weathering and dismantling.","es":"Relieve con aspecto de ruinas por meteorización y desmantelamiento."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/collado","prefLabel":{"en":"pass; col","es":"collado; puerto; col"},"definition":{"en":"A depression in a divide allowing passage.","es":"Depresión en una divisoria que permite el paso."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/collado-poligenetico","prefLabel":{"en":"pass; col","es":"collado poligenetico"},"altLabel":{"es":["puerto; col"]},"definition":{"en":"A depression in a divide allowing passage.","es":"Depresión en una divisoria que permite el paso."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/depresion-cerrada-o-semicerrada-de-origen-mixto","prefLabel":{"en":"closed or semi-closed depression of mixed origin","es":"depresión cerrada o semicerrada de origen mixto"},"definition":{"en":"Closed topographic depression originated by multiple processes.","es":"Depresión topográfica cerrada originada por procesos múltiples."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/domo","prefLabel":{"en":"dome","es":"domo"},"definition":{"en":"A rounded elevation formed by extrusion of viscous lava.","es":"Elevación redondeada formada por extrusión de lava viscosa."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/domo-endogeno","prefLabel":{"en":"endogenous dome","es":"domo endógeno"},"definition":{"en":"A volcanic dome formed by magma injection that uplifts surface layers.","es":"Domo volcánico formado por inyección de magma que levanta las capas superficiales."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/domo-exogeno","prefLabel":{"en":"exogenous dome","es":"domo exógeno"},"definition":{"en":"A volcanic dome formed by lava extrusion at the surface.","es":"Domo volcánico formado por extrusión de lava en superficie."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe","prefLabel":{"en":"scarp","es":"escarpe"},"definition":{"en":"An abrupt slope of polygenetic origin.","es":"Talud abrupto de origen poligénico."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/fondo-de-valle-de-origen-mixto","prefLabel":{"en":"mixed-origin valley floor","es":"fondo de valle de origen mixto"},"definition":{"en":"Valley floor formed by combined fluvial and gravitational processes.","es":"Fondo de valle formado por procesos fluviales y gravitacionales combinados."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/glacis-de-cobertera-pedimento-cubierto-glacis-mixto","prefLabel":{"en":"covered glacis; covered pediment","es":"glacis de cobertera; pedimento cubierto; glacis mixto"},"definition":{"en":"A glacis covered by a thin mantle of sediments.","es":"Glacis cubierto por un manto delgado de sedimentos."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/glacis-de-cobertera-degradado-o-disectado","prefLabel":{"en":"degraded or dissected covered glacis","es":"glacis de cobertera degradado o disectado"},"definition":{"en":"A covered glacis incised by channels.","es":"Glacis de cobertera incidido por cauces."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/glacis-de-erosion-pediment","prefLabel":{"en":"erosion glacis; pediment","es":"glacis de erosión; pediment"},"definition":{"en":"Gently inclined erosion surface at the foot of a relief.","es":"Superficie suavemente inclinada de erosión al pie de un relieve."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/glacis-de-erosion-degradado","prefLabel":{"en":"degraded erosion glacis","es":"glacis de erosión degradado"},"definition":{"en":"An erosion glacis modified by subsequent erosional processes.","es":"Glacis de erosión modificado por procesos erosivos posteriores."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/glacis-de-vertiente-glacis-coluvial","prefLabel":{"en":"slope glacis; colluvial glacis","es":"glacis de vertiente; glacis coluvial"},"definition":{"en":"A glacis formed by colluvial deposits at the foot of a slope.","es":"Glacis formado por depósitos coluviales al pie de una vertiente."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/hombrera","prefLabel":{"en":"shoulder; bench","es":"hombrera; rellano"},"definition":{"en":"A subhorizontal surface interrupting a slope.","es":"Superficie subhorizontal que interrumpe una pendiente."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/hombrera-poligenetica","prefLabel":{"en":"shoulder; bench","es":"hombrera poligenética"},"definition":{"en":"A subhorizontal surface interrupting a slope.","es":"Superficie subhorizontal que interrumpe una pendiente."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/monte-isla-relieve-aislado-inselberg","prefLabel":{"en":"inselberg","es":"monte isla, relieve aislado; inselberg"},"definition":{"en":"Isolated steep-walled relief rising above a plain.","es":"Relieve aislado de paredes empinadas que se eleva sobre una llanura."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/monte-isla-con-acanaladuras","prefLabel":{"en":"fluted inselberg","es":"monte isla con acanaladuras"},"definition":{"en":"An inselberg with vertical grooves on its walls.","es":"Inselberg con surcos verticales en sus paredes."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/monte-isla-con-derrubios","prefLabel":{"en":"debris-mantled inselberg","es":"monte isla con derrubios"},"definition":{"en":"An inselberg partially covered by debris.","es":"Inselberg parcialmente cubierto por derrubios."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/monte-isla-con-descamacion","prefLabel":{"en":"exfoliating inselberg","es":"monte isla con descamación"},"definition":{"en":"An inselberg with rock exfoliation in sheets.","es":"Inselberg con descamación de la roca en láminas."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/monte-isla-de-cumbre-plana","prefLabel":{"en":"flat-topped inselberg","es":"monte isla de cumbre plana"},"definition":{"en":"An inselberg with a flattened summit.","es":"Inselberg con la cima aplanada."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/monte-isla-lineal-cresta-barra","prefLabel":{"en":"linear inselberg; ridge","es":"monte isla lineal; cresta; barra"},"definition":{"en":"An elongated and narrow inselberg.","es":"Inselberg de forma alargada y estrecha."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/monticulo-loma","prefLabel":{"en":"hillock; knoll","es":"montículo; loma"},"definition":{"en":"A small gentle terrain elevation.","es":"Pequeña elevación suave del terreno."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/otros-depositos","prefLabel":{"en":"other deposits","es":"otros depósitos"},"definition":{"en":"Deposits not classified in the previous categories.","es":"Depósitos no clasificados en las categorías anteriores."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/pico-principal-aguja-horn","prefLabel":{"en":"main peak; horn","es":"pico principal; aguja; horn"},"definition":{"en":"Sharp and prominent summit in a polygenetic relief.","es":"Cima aguda y prominente en un relieve poligénico."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/reborde-de-deposito-g