r productos de alteración residual."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/superficie-de-erosion-degradada","prefLabel":{"en":"degraded erosion surface","es":"superficie de erosión degradada"},"definition":{"en":"An erosion surface modified by subsequent erosional processes.","es":"Superficie de erosión modificada por procesos erosivos posteriores."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/techo-de-piedemonte-ranya","prefLabel":{"en":"piedmont surface; raña","es":"techo de piedemonte; raña"},"definition":{"en":"Culminating surface of a piedmont, often covered by coarse detrital deposits.","es":"Superficie culminante de un piedemonte, a menudo cubierta por depósitos detríticos gruesos."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/superficie-de-erosion-con-alterita","prefLabel":{"en":"erosion surface with alterite","es":"superficie de erosión con alterita"},"definition":{"en":"An erosion surface covered by residual weathering products.","es":"Superficie de erosión cubierta por productos de alteración residual."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/superficie-de-erosion-degradada","prefLabel":{"en":"degraded erosion surface","es":"superficie de erosión degradada"},"definition":{"en":"An erosion surface modified by subsequent erosional processes.","es":"Superficie de erosión modificada por procesos erosivos posteriores."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/superficie-de-erosion-poligenetica","prefLabel":{"en":"erosion surface","es":"superficie de erosión poligenética"},"definition":{"en":"A planation surface produced by prolonged erosion.","es":"Superficie de aplanamiento producida por erosión prolongada."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/superficie-de-erosion-con-alterita","prefLabel":{"en":"erosion surface with alterite","es":"superficie de erosión con alterita"},"definition":{"en":"An erosion surface covered by residual weathering products.","es":"Superficie de erosión cubierta por productos de alteración residual."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/superficie-de-erosion-degradada","prefLabel":{"en":"degraded erosion surface","es":"superficie de erosión degradada"},"definition":{"en":"An erosion surface modified by subsequent erosional processes.","es":"Superficie de erosión modificada por procesos erosivos posteriores."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/techo-de-piedemonte-ranya","prefLabel":{"en":"piedmont surface; raña","es":"techo de piedemonte; raña"},"definition":{"en":"Culminating surface of a piedmont, often covered by coarse detrital deposits.","es":"Superficie culminante de un piedemonte, a menudo cubierta por depósitos detríticos gruesos."}}]}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/pedimento","prefLabel":{"en":"pediment","es":"pedimento"},"definition":{"en":"A gently sloping erosional surface developed at the foot of a receding hill or mountain slope, commonly with a slightly concave-upward profile, that cross-cuts rock or sediment strata that extend beneath adjacent uplands.","es":"Superficie erosiva de baja pendiente desarrollada al pie de un relieve montañoso, generalmente con un perfil algo cóncavo hacia arriba, que corta los estratos de roca o de sedimentos que se extienden bajo las tierras altas adyacentes."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/pendiente-de-cabecera","prefLabel":{"en":"head slope","es":"pendiente de cabecera"},"definition":{"en":"A geomorphologic component of hills consisting of a laterally concave area of a hillside, especially at the head of a drainage way, resulting in converging overland water flow.","es":"Elemento geomorfológico de una colina constituido por un área de la ladera lateralmente cóncava, especialmente en la cabecera de una vía de drenaje, que determina que las corrientes de agua sean convergentes."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/relicto","prefLabel":{"en":"relic","es":"relicto"},"definition":{"en":"A landform that has survived decay or disintegration, or one that has been left behind after the disappearance of the greater part of its substance such as a remnant island.","es":"Forma de relieve que ha sobrevivido a la degradación o desintegración, o que ha permanecido tras desaparecer la mayor parte del material subyacente, como por ejemplo, un monte isla."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/superficie-de-erosion","prefLabel":{"en":"erosion surface","es":"superficie de erosión"},"definition":{"en":"Geomorphologic landscapes and landforms related dominantly to water erosion but excluding perennial channel flow (i.e. fluvial, glaciofluvial) or eolian erosion.","es":"Paisajes geomorfológicos y formas del relieve relacionados predominantemente con la erosión del agua, con exclusión de las corrientes canalizadas perennes (es decir, fluviales, glaciofluviales), o a la erosión eólica."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cerro-conico","prefLabel":{"en":"conical hill","es":"cerro cónico"},"definition":{"en":"A conical terrain elevation.","es":"Elevación del terreno de forma cónica."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cerro-conico-poligenetico","prefLabel":{"en":"conical hill","es":"cerro cónico poligenético"},"definition":{"en":"A conical terrain elevation.","es":"Elevación del terreno de forma cónica."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cerro-ruiniforme-caos-de-bloques","prefLabel":{"en":"ruiniform hill; block chaos","es":"cerro ruiniforme poligenetico"},"altLabel":{"es":["caos de bloques"]},"definition":{"en":"Relief with a ruin-like appearance due to weathering and dismantling.","es":"Relieve con aspecto de ruinas por meteorización y desmantelamiento."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/collado","prefLabel":{"en":"pass; col","es":"collado; puerto; col"},"definition":{"en":"A depression in a divide allowing passage.","es":"Depresión en una divisoria que permite el paso."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/collado-poligenetico","prefLabel":{"en":"pass; col","es":"collado poligenetico"},"altLabel":{"es":["puerto; col"]},"definition":{"en":"A depression in a divide allowing passage.","es":"Depresión en una divisoria que permite el paso."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/depresion-cerrada-o-semicerrada-de-origen-mixto","prefLabel":{"en":"closed or semi-closed depression of mixed origin","es":"depresión cerrada o semicerrada de origen mixto"},"definition":{"en":"Closed topographic depression originated by multiple processes.","es":"Depresión topográfica cerrada originada por procesos múltiples."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/domo","prefLabel":{"en":"dome","es":"domo"},"definition":{"en":"A rounded elevation formed by extrusion of viscous lava.","es":"Elevación redondeada formada por extrusión de lava viscosa."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/domo-endogeno","prefLabel":{"en":"endogenous dome","es":"domo endógeno"},"definition":{"en":"A volcanic dome formed by magma injection that uplifts surface layers.","es":"Domo volcánico formado por inyección de magma que levanta las capas superficiales."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/domo-exogeno","prefLabel":{"en":"exogenous dome","es":"domo exógeno"},"definition":{"en":"A volcanic dome formed by lava extrusion at the surface.","es":"Domo volcánico formado por extrusión de lava en superficie."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe","prefLabel":{"en":"scarp","es":"escarpe"},"definition":{"en":"An abrupt slope of polygenetic origin.","es":"Talud abrupto de origen poligénico."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/fondo-de-valle-de-origen-mixto","prefLabel":{"en":"mixed-origin valley floor","es":"fondo de valle de origen mixto"},"definition":{"en":"Valley floor formed by combined fluvial and gravitational processes.","es":"Fondo de valle formado por procesos fluviales y gravitacionales combinados."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/glacis-de-cobertera-pedimento-cubierto-glacis-mixto","prefLabel":{"en":"covered glacis; covered pediment","es":"glacis de cobertera; pedimento cubierto; glacis mixto"},"definition":{"en":"A glacis covered by a thin mantle of sediments.","es":"Glacis cubierto por un manto delgado de sedimentos."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/glacis-de-cobertera-degradado-o-disectado","prefLabel":{"en":"degraded or dissected covered glacis","es":"glacis de cobertera degradado o disectado"},"definition":{"en":"A covered glacis incised by channels.","es":"Glacis de cobertera incidido por cauces."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/glacis-de-erosion-pediment","prefLabel":{"en":"erosion glacis; pediment","es":"glacis de erosión; pediment"},"definition":{"en":"Gently inclined erosion surface at the foot of a relief.","es":"Superficie suavemente inclinada de erosión al pie de un relieve."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/glacis-de-erosion-degradado","prefLabel":{"en":"degraded erosion glacis","es":"glacis de erosión degradado"},"definition":{"en":"An erosion glacis modified by subsequent erosional processes.","es":"Glacis de erosión modificado por procesos erosivos posteriores."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/glacis-de-vertiente-glacis-coluvial","prefLabel":{"en":"slope glacis; colluvial glacis","es":"glacis de vertiente; glacis coluvial"},"definition":{"en":"A glacis formed by colluvial deposits at the foot of a slope.","es":"Glacis formado por depósitos coluviales al pie de una vertiente."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/hombrera","prefLabel":{"en":"shoulder; bench","es":"hombrera; rellano"},"definition":{"en":"A subhorizontal surface interrupting a slope.","es":"Superficie subhorizontal que interrumpe una pendiente."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/hombrera-poligenetica","prefLabel":{"en":"shoulder; bench","es":"hombrera poligenética"},"definition":{"en":"A subhorizontal surface interrupting a slope.","es":"Superficie subhorizontal que interrumpe una pendiente."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/monte-isla-relieve-aislado-inselberg","prefLabel":{"en":"inselberg","es":"monte isla, relieve aislado; inselberg"},"definition":{"en":"Isolated steep-walled relief rising above a plain.","es":"Relieve aislado de paredes empinadas que se eleva sobre una llanura."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/monte-isla-con-acanaladuras","prefLabel":{"en":"fluted inselberg","es":"monte isla con acanaladuras"},"definition":{"en":"An inselberg with vertical grooves on its walls.","es":"Inselberg con surcos verticales en sus paredes."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/monte-isla-con-derrubios","prefLabel":{"en":"debris-mantled inselberg","es":"monte isla con derrubios"},"definition":{"en":"An inselberg partially covered by debris.","es":"Inselberg parcialmente cubierto por derrubios."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/monte-isla-con-descamacion","prefLabel":{"en":"exfoliating inselberg","es":"monte isla con descamación"},"definition":{"en":"An inselberg with rock exfoliation in sheets.","es":"Inselberg con descamación de la roca en láminas."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/monte-isla-de-cumbre-plana","prefLabel":{"en":"flat-topped inselberg","es":"monte isla de cumbre plana"},"definition":{"en":"An inselberg with a flattened summit.","es":"Inselberg con la cima aplanada."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/monte-isla-lineal-cresta-barra","prefLabel":{"en":"linear inselberg; ridge","es":"monte isla lineal; cresta; barra"},"definition":{"en":"An elongated and narrow inselberg.","es":"Inselberg de forma alargada y estrecha."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/monticulo-loma","prefLabel":{"en":"hillock; knoll","es":"montículo; loma"},"definition":{"en":"A small gentle terrain elevation.","es":"Pequeña elevación suave del terreno."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/otros-depositos","prefLabel":{"en":"other deposits","es":"otros depósitos"},"definition":{"en":"Deposits not classified in the previous categories.","es":"Depósitos no clasificados en las categorías anteriores."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/pico-principal-aguja-horn","prefLabel":{"en":"main peak; horn","es":"pico principal; aguja; horn"},"definition":{"en":"Sharp and prominent summit in a polygenetic relief.","es":"Cima aguda y prominente en un relieve poligénico."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/reborde-de-deposito-glacis","prefLabel":{"en":"deposit edge (glacis)","es":"reborde de depósito (glacis)"},"definition":{"en":"Edge of a glacis or piedmont deposit.","es":"Borde de un depósito de glacis o piedemonte."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/relieve-residual-monadnok","prefLabel":{"en":"residual relief; monadnock","es":"relieve residual; monadnok"},"definition":{"en":"Isolated relief rising above an erosion surface.","es":"Relieve aislado que sobresale de una superficie de erosión."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/superficie-de-cumbres-cresta-apalachiana","prefLabel":{"en":"summit surface; Appalachian ridge","es":"superficie de cumbres; cresta apalachiana"},"definition":{"en":"A summit surface maintaining a homogeneous altitude.","es":"Superficie de cumbres que mantiene una altitud homogénea."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/superficie-de-erosion","prefLabel":{"en":"erosion surface","es":"superficie de erosión"},"definition":{"en":"Geomorphologic landscapes and landforms related dominantly to water erosion but excluding perennial channel flow (i.e. fluvial, glaciofluvial) or eolian erosion.","es":"Paisajes geomorfológicos y formas del relieve relacionados predominantemente con la erosión del agua, con exclusión de las corrientes canalizadas perennes (es decir, fluviales, glaciofluviales), o a la erosión eólica."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cerro-conico","prefLabel":{"en":"conical hill","es":"cerro cónico"},"definition":{"en":"A conical terrain elevation.","es":"Elevación del terreno de forma cónica."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cerro-conico-poligenetico","prefLabel":{"en":"conical hill","es":"cerro cónico poligenético"},"definition":{"en":"A conical terrain elevation.","es":"Elevación del terreno de forma cónica."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/cerro-ruiniforme-caos-de-bloques","prefLabel":{"en":"ruiniform hill; block chaos","es":"cerro ruiniforme poligenetico"},"altLabel":{"es":["caos de bloques"]},"definition":{"en":"Relief with a ruin-like appearance due to weathering and dismantling.","es":"Relieve con aspecto de ruinas por meteorización y desmantelamiento."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/collado","prefLabel":{"en":"pass; col","es":"collado; puerto; col"},"definition":{"en":"A depression in a divide allowing passage.","es":"Depresión en una divisoria que permite el paso."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/collado-poligenetico","prefLabel":{"en":"pass; col","es":"collado poligenetico"},"altLabel":{"es":["puerto; col"]},"definition":{"en":"A depression in a divide allowing passage.","es":"Depresión en una divisoria que permite el paso."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/depresion-cerrada-o-semicerrada-de-origen-mixto","prefLabel":{"en":"closed or semi-closed depression of mixed origin","es":"depresión cerrada o semicerrada de origen mixto"},"definition":{"en":"Closed topographic depression originated by multiple processes.","es":"Depresión topográfica cerrada originada por procesos múltiples."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/domo","prefLabel":{"en":"dome","es":"domo"},"definition":{"en":"A rounded elevation formed by extrusion of viscous lava.","es":"Elevación redondeada formada por extrusión de lava viscosa."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/domo-endogeno","prefLabel":{"en":"endogenous dome","es":"domo endógeno"},"definition":{"en":"A volcanic dome formed by magma injection that uplifts surface layers.","es":"Domo volcánico formado por inyección de magma que levanta las capas superficiales."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/domo-exogeno","prefLabel":{"en":"exogenous dome","es":"domo exógeno"},"definition":{"en":"A volcanic dome formed by lava extrusion at the surface.","es":"Domo volcánico formado por extrusión de lava en superficie."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe","prefLabel":{"en":"scarp","es":"escarpe"},"definition":{"en":"An abrupt slope of polygenetic origin.","es":"Talud abrupto de origen poligénico."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/fondo-de-valle-de-origen-mixto","prefLabel":{"en":"mixed-origin valley floor","es":"fondo de valle de origen mixto"},"definition":{"en":"Valley floor formed by combined fluvial and gravitational processes.","es":"Fondo de valle formado por procesos fluviales y gravitacionales combinados."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/glacis-de-cobertera-pedimento-cubierto-glacis-mixto","prefLabel":{"en":"covered glacis; covered pediment","es":"glacis de cobertera; pedimento cubierto; glacis mixto"},"definition":{"en":"A glacis covered by a thin mantle of sediments.","es":"Glacis cubierto por un manto delgado de sedimentos."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/glacis-de-cobertera-degradado-o-disectado","prefLabel":{"en":"degraded or dissected covered glacis","es":"glacis de cobertera degradado o disectado"},"definition":{"en":"A covered glacis incised by channels.","es":"Glacis de cobertera incidido por cauces."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/glacis-de-erosion-pediment","prefLabel":{"en":"erosion glacis; pediment","es":"glacis de erosión; pediment"},"definition":{"en":"Gently inclined erosion surface at the foot of a relief.","es":"Superficie suavemente inclinada de erosión al pie de un relieve."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/glacis-de-erosion-degradado","prefLabel":{"en":"degraded erosion glacis","es":"glacis de erosión degradado"},"definition":{"en":"An erosion glacis modified by subsequent erosional processes.","es":"Glacis de erosión modificado por procesos erosivos 