n aspecto de ruinas por meteorización y desmantelamiento."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/collado","prefLabel":{"en":"pass; col","es":"collado; puerto; col"},"definition":{"en":"A depression in a divide allowing passage.","es":"Depresión en una divisoria que permite el paso."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/collado-poligenetico","prefLabel":{"en":"pass; col","es":"collado poligenetico"},"altLabel":{"es":["puerto; col"]},"definition":{"en":"A depression in a divide allowing passage.","es":"Depresión en una divisoria que permite el paso."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/depresion-cerrada-o-semicerrada-de-origen-mixto","prefLabel":{"en":"closed or semi-closed depression of mixed origin","es":"depresión cerrada o semicerrada de origen mixto"},"definition":{"en":"Closed topographic depression originated by multiple processes.","es":"Depresión topográfica cerrada originada por procesos múltiples."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/domo","prefLabel":{"en":"dome","es":"domo"},"definition":{"en":"A rounded elevation formed by extrusion of viscous lava.","es":"Elevación redondeada formada por extrusión de lava viscosa."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/domo-endogeno","prefLabel":{"en":"endogenous dome","es":"domo endógeno"},"definition":{"en":"A volcanic dome formed by magma injection that uplifts surface layers.","es":"Domo volcánico formado por inyección de magma que levanta las capas superficiales."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/domo-exogeno","prefLabel":{"en":"exogenous dome","es":"domo exógeno"},"definition":{"en":"A volcanic dome formed by lava extrusion at the surface.","es":"Domo volcánico formado por extrusión de lava en superficie."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/escarpe","prefLabel":{"en":"scarp","es":"escarpe"},"definition":{"en":"An abrupt slope of polygenetic origin.","es":"Talud abrupto de origen poligénico."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/fondo-de-valle-de-origen-mixto","prefLabel":{"en":"mixed-origin valley floor","es":"fondo de valle de origen mixto"},"definition":{"en":"Valley floor formed by combined fluvial and gravitational processes.","es":"Fondo de valle formado por procesos fluviales y gravitacionales combinados."}},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/glacis-de-cobertera-pedimento-cubierto-glacis-mixto","prefLabel":{"en":"covered glacis; covered pediment","es":"glacis de cobertera; pedimento cubierto; glacis mixto"},"definition":{"en":"A glacis covered by a thin mantle of sediments.","es":"Glacis cubierto por un manto delgado de sedimentos."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/glacis-de-cobertera-degradado-o-disectado","prefLabel":{"en":"degraded or dissected covered glacis","es":"glacis de cobertera degradado o disectado"},"definition":{"en":"A covered glacis incised by channels.","es":"Glacis de cobertera incidido por cauces."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/glacis-de-erosion-pediment","prefLabel":{"en":"erosion glacis; pediment","es":"glacis de erosión; pediment"},"definition":{"en":"Gently inclined erosion surface at the foot of a relief.","es":"Superficie suavemente inclinada de erosión al pie de un relieve."},"narrower":[{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/geomorfologia-tipo-natural/glacis-de-erosion-degradado","prefLabel":{"en":"degraded erosion glacis","es":"glacis de erosión degradado"},"definition":{"en":"An erosion glacis modified by subsequent erosional processes.","es":"Glacis de erosión modificado por procesos erosivos posteriores."}}]},{"id":"https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios